( 5... Be7
{ The bishop retreats to its safest square. White plays [d4], and Black's best is [b:Na5]!, hitting the bishop on c4 so that Black can return the pawn on good terms. This was Anand's choice against Kasparov; their game at Riga in 1995 brought the Evans back to top level. After [w:Be2] [b:exd4] [w:Qxd4] White has a lead in development for the pawn, and the queen on d4 eyes g7. Black must not play passively with [b:d6] and [b:Nh6]: the bishop on c1 takes on h6. [%csl Ye7][%cal Gd2d4,Bc6a5] }
