( 6... d6
{ This symmetrical tabiya of the Four Knights Italian arises in millions of games. Because both kings have castled and d6 is on the board, White cannot easily blast open the centre with [w:d4], so piece play decides. [Na4] goes straight after Black's dark-squared bishop on c5 to secure the bishop pair, [Bg5] pins the f6 knight to set up [w:Nd5] pressure, and [h3] rules out [b:Bg4] before [w:Be3]. [%cal Gc3a4,Gc1g5,Gh2h3] }
