{ Black has castled and asks the bishop to decide. [Bh4] is the simple retreat, keeping the pin, and [Bxf6] gives up the bishop for the knight, which is fine too. The famous trick here is [w:h4], the fishing pole: White leaves the bishop hanging so that after [b:hxg5] [w:hxg5] the h-file opens against Black's king. Against the right defence it loses a piece, but if Black's knight retreats to h7, [w:g6] wins, because the pawn on f7 is pinned by the bishop on c4. [%cal Gg5h4,Gg5f6,Rh2h4] }
