{ The fishing pole: White offers the bishop to open the h-file, and with the rook still on h1 the idea looks deadly. Many club players fall for it. But after [hxg5 hxg5 Ng4] Black's knight jumps to safety with gain of time, hitting f2, and if White pushes [w:g6] Black has [b:Bxf2+] and then the king or queen joins the defence. White is simply a piece down. The quiet [Bh4] was the move; the trap only works against a careless reply. }
