{ The Italian Gambit. Black's best is [Bxd4]!: after [w:Nxd4] [b:Nxd4] Black is a pawn up, and White's attack with [w:f4] or [w:c3] is not quite enough. Unzicker recommended it. [exd4] is the Scotch Gambit, also good. Taking with the knight is dangerous: after [w:Nxe5] only [b:Qe7] holds, because f7 is attacked twice. White plays this gambit for quick development, so Black should look for moves that keep the extra pawn and finish developing. [%cal Gc5d4,Ge5d4,Rc6d4] }
