5... Qe7 ) ) 4... Nf6 5. d3 ( 5. d4
{ White strikes in the centre, and Black must take: [exd4] is the only good move. Any retreat, such as [b:Bb6], lets [w:dxe5] hit the knight on f6, and Black loses time while White's pawns take over the centre. After [exd4] White chooses between recapturing with [w:cxd4], the main line where Black answers with the check [b:Bb4+], and the sharper [w:e5] or [w:O-O], where White offers a pawn for a lead in development. In all these lines Black's freeing move is [b:d5]. [%csl Rb6][%cal Ge5d4] }
