{ The modern attack: White kicks the knight before recapturing on d4. Black's answer is [d5]!, hitting the bishop on c4, so that the knight can go to e4 next with a pawn behind it. Other moves fail. On g4 the knight is cut off after [w:cxd4] and [w:h3], and on e4 at once it runs into [w:Bd5]. After [d5] White's best is [w:Bb5], pinning the knight on c6, and the game stays balanced. The same pawn break answers [w:e5] in almost every line of the Italian. [%cal Gd7d5,Gf6e4] }
