{ The main line of the Pianissimo. Black's pawn holds e5, and now [b:Na5] threatens to trade off White's best bishop. White prepares for it with [Bb3] or [a4], or castles first with [O-O]. Black usually waits with the king in the centre, ready for [b:h6] and [b:g5] if White castles too early or plays [w:h3], or castles once White's plan is clear. Both sides take their time: there is no contact between the pieces yet, and the first player to commit often gives the other a target. [%cal Ge1g1,Gc4b3,Ga2a4,Rc6a5] }
