{ The Giuoco Pianissimo, the 'very quiet game' and the most played line at the top today. White keeps the centre closed and builds up: [w:O-O], [w:Re1], [w:Bb3], [w:h3] and the knight tour [w:Nbd2]-f1-g3, before [w:d4] or an attack on the kingside. The pawn on c3 prepares [w:d4] and gives the bishop a retreat on c2 against [b:Na5]. Black answers with [d6] or [O-O], and often [a6] with [b:Ba7], keeping the bishop out of reach of the d-pawn. [%cal Gb1d2,Gd2f1,Gf1g3] }
( 5. d4 exd4 6. cxd4
{ White has the ideal centre, and the bishop on c5 is attacked. The check [Bb4+] is the only good move. It gains a tempo for [b:Nxe4] or [b:d5] before the pawns can roll forward, and it makes White decide how to block: with the bishop, a knight, or the king. A quiet retreat lets White push [w:e5] or [w:d5] and gain more space with tempo on Black's knights, and Black is cramped for a long time. The rule of this line: Black must hit the centre before White's pawns advance. [%cal Gc5b4,Gb4e1] }
