8... Nxb4
{ The bishops are gone and Black is a pawn up, but both Black knights are loose. [Bxf7+]! is the point: after [b:Kxf7] [w:Qb3+] the queen checks and hits the knight on b4, and White wins back the pawn. The game is then level, with Black's king displaced but safe enough. Quiet moves give Black time to tidy up and keep the extra pawn: [w:Qe2], pinning the knight on e4, looks strong, but after [b:d5] or [b:Qe7] Black holds everything, and White is simply a pawn down. [%csl Yb4][%cal Gc4f7,Gd1b3] }
