{ The modern line. The bishop on d3 controls e4, so the plan of [b:e4] needs preparation. Black's best is [Nd5]!: the knight heads for f4, where it hits the bishop and g2. After [w:Nf3] [b:Bd6] [w:O-O] [b:Nf4] the game is balanced. [h6] is also fine, kicking the knight first; then [w:Ne4] trades it off. The structure suits players who like slow play with a pawn more. [%cal Gf6d5,Gh7h6,Bd5f4] }
