{ The check must be blocked or avoided. [Be6] is the main move: it develops and keeps d5 covered for the queen, and after [w:Ng5] [b:Qd5] [w:Nc3] [b:Qf5] the old main line of the Max Lange follows. [Kf8] is the other way: the king steps aside, but after [w:Bg5] and [w:fxg7+] it ends up on g7 or g8, in the open. Blocking with the queen or the knight loses material. Black's bishop on e6 will be attacked again and again, so Black must keep it protected. [%csl Ye8][%cal Gc8e6,Ge8f8] }
