{ Taking back with the queen is a classic slip in the Scotch. The pawn on d4 was defended by the knight on c6, so [Nxd4] wins the queen for a knight, and the game is practically over. The queen only goes to d4 once that knight has been traded off, as in the Lolli Variation. The normal recapture is with the knight from f3, which develops a piece and keeps the queen safe at home. }
