{ This is a trap line that scores well in fast games. White hopes for [h6]: after [h6 Nxf7 Kxf7 Bc4+], the natural [b:Ke8] walks into a forced mate starting with a queen check on h5. But the knight move breaks every opening rule, and Black punishes it calmly with [Be7], hitting the knight: the attack on f7 falls apart and Black keeps the extra pawn. [d5] is also strong. Black is clearly better. }
