( 7... O-O 8. O-O
{ Both kings are safe. Black's best plans keep the bishop on the a7-g1 diagonal. [b6] supports it on c5 and prepares [Bb7]; later Black can trade on d4 and bring the knight to f5. [Bb6] steps out of any trick on d4 at once. A slow [d6] is playable too, but the bishop on c5 then needs watching. [%csl Yc5][%cal Gb7b6,Gc5b6] }
