{ Castling forgets that the bishop on c4 was attacked by the knight on e5, and nothing defends it. [Nxc4] wins it for nothing. In these lines the knight on e5 is always looking at c4, d3 and f3, so every move must answer that. White had to move the bishop first, to e2, where it also covers f3 and g4, or to b3, and castle afterwards. }
