{ Blumenfeld's [Qg6] forks two targets at once, hitting both g2 and the central pawn on e4 to test White's nerve. The calm, grandmaster answer is [O-O]: castling shelters g2 with the king and rook while deliberately leaving e4 poisoned, since [O-O Qxe4 Nd2 Qg6 f4] (or [Bf3]) gives White a huge lead in piece activity against Black's uncastled king. Kicking the e5 knight with the f-pawn before castling loosens White's own dark squares. [%csl Yg2,Ye4,Ye5][%cal Ge1g1] }
