8. Re1 ) ) ) ( 5... dxc6 ) ( 5... Bxf2+ $4
{ A check, but with no follow-up. [Kxf2] takes the bishop, and the knight on c6 still attacks Black's queen, so Black must deal with that too. Black has given a bishop for a pawn and gained nothing. A check on f2 is only good if it wins something, like a queen or a rook. Here the in-between move with the queen to f6, threatening mate, was the real way to use the pressure on f2. }
