{ White covers f2 with the queen and keeps the queens on. Now Black takes the knight back. [dxc6] is the main move: it opens the bishop on c8 and keeps Black's pawns sound enough, with a quick plan of the bishop to e6, the knight to e7 and long castling. [bxc6] keeps a central pawn for [d5] and is equally playable. White will develop with [Nc3] and [Bd3], castle short, and use the healthier kingside majority. [%csl Yc6,Yf2][%cal Gd7c6,Gb7c6] }
