{ White has finished the first wave of development. Black's main plans are [Be6], preparing long castling, when White often chases the bishop on c5 with [Na4]; [Bd4], planting the bishop in the center; and [Ne7], heading for g6 and short castling. The position is balanced: Black's pieces are active, and the only long-term worry is structure, since in an endgame White's kingside majority can make a passed pawn while Black's doubled c-pawns can't. Keep an eye on f2: it is attacked twice and defended twice, so captures there only work if White's queen leaves d2. [%csl Yf2][%cal Gc8e6,Gc5d4,Gg8e7] }
