{ In this Mieses-style line where Black met 5.[Nxc6] with the intermediate mate threat 5.[Qf6], [Be6] completes queenside development and prepares [b:Rd8] with tempo against White's queen on d2. [Na4] is White's cleanest plan, hunting down the active c5 bishop so White secures the bishop pair to press against Black's doubled c-pawns over the long haul. Black stays fully competitive by keeping pieces active with [b:Be7], [b:Bd6], or long castling. [%cal Gc3a4] }
