{ Black defends c7 in a tricky way: grabbing it would let Black mate on f2, so White must first take care of f2. [Qe2] and [Qf3] both defend it, and both also protect e4. After that, the fork on c7 is a real threat again, and Black usually answers with [Kd8] or retreats the queen with [Qd8]. White has a pleasant lead in development, but Black's position holds. The big trap here is to take on c7 at once. [%csl Rf2,Yc7][%cal Gd1e2,Gd1f3] }
