( 8. Ng5
{ The knight joins the attack on f7 with the bishop on c4, while the bishop on b2 still aims at g7 behind the knight on f6. Black's best is [O-O], castling straight into the storm but getting the king off the e-file: after [O-O e5 Nxe5], the Hanneken Variation, Black gives back material to break the attack, and the game is balanced. Other moves lose f7, and with it the kingside, since Black's king would be stuck in the center facing every white piece. [%csl Rf7,Yg7][%cal Ge8g8] }
