{ The Benima Defense, also reached from the Hungarian Defense of the Italian Game. Black doesn't fight for the pawn on d4 and simply prepares to develop and castle. It is solid but passive: the bishop on e7 does little, and White can take back with [Nxd4], reaching a comfortable Scotch-type position. [O-O] and [c3] keep gambit options open. Black's usual plan is [Nf6], [d6] and castling, then a break with [d5] when it becomes possible. [%csl Yd4][%cal Gf3d4,Ge1g1,Gc2c3] }
