{ The Zaitsev System, Igor Zaitsev's dynamic creation that Anatoly Karpov defended across his World Championship matches against Garry Kasparov. Without spending two moves rerouting a knight, Black puts immediate pressure on e4 with [Bb7], [b:Re8], and [b:Bf8]. White strikes in the center with [d4] (or plays [d3]), and after [d4 Re8] can either repeat moves with [w:Ng5] against f7 or play on with [w:Nbd2]. [%csl Ye4,Yf7][%cal Gd2d4] }
