{ With both the b7-bishop and e8-rook bearing down on e4, Black leaves f7 guarded only by the king, inviting the well-known Zaitsev repetition ([Ng5 Rf8 Nf3 Re8]) if both players are content with a draw. To fight for an advantage, White defends e4 with [Nbd2] ([Nbd2 Bf8 a4 h6 Bc2 exd4 cxd4 Nb4 Bb1 c5 d5]) or [Bc2]; developing the bishop to g5 fails to protect e4. [%csl Ye4,Yf7,Yg5][%cal Gb1d2] }
