11... Nxe4 12. Bxe7 Nxe7 13. Bc2 ) 11... Bf8
{ Black's bishop drops back to f8, uncovering the rook on e8 against e4 while reinforcing g7 and preparing [b:g6]. Because Black now threatens [b:exd4] followed by [b:Nxe4] winning White's central pawn, White cannot continue the knight tour to f1 yet: White either challenges the queenside right away with [a4] ([a4 h6 Bc2 exd4 cxd4 Nb4 Bb1 c5]), overprotects e4 with [Bc2], or closes the center with [d5]. [%csl Yf8,Ye8,Ye4][%cal Ga2a4] }
12. a4 ( 12. Bc2 ) ( 12. d5 ) ( 12. Nf1 $6
