12... exd4 13. cxd4 Na5 14. Bc2 Nxe4 ) ) ( 9... h6
{ The Smyslov Variation, Vasily Smyslov's solid refinement of the Closed Spanish. Playing [h6] takes g5 away from White's knight and c1-bishop in advance, so that after [d4] and [b:Re8] White has no [w:Ng5] harassment against f7 to force a repetition or disrupt Black's coordination. Black then regroups smoothly with [b:Bf8], [b:Bb7] or [b:Bd7], and [b:g6] with [b:Bg7]; [d3] is White's quieter alternative. [%csl Yg5,Yf7][%cal Gd2d4] }
