{ Black surrenders the e5 strongpoint at once, opening the d- and e-files so the light-squared bishop on c8 and queen on d8 gain immediate scope as compensation for the doubled c-pawns. White almost always recaptures with [Qxd4], Lasker's move, centralizing the queen with an eye on g7 and inviting [Qxd4 Qxd4 Nxd4], where White's healthy 4-vs-3 kingside majority faces Black's bishop pair. Recapturing with the knight via [Nxd4] keeps queens on the board, though Black gets brisk counterplay with [Nxd4 c5] and [b:Bd6] or [b:Be6]. [%csl Yd4,Yg7][%cal Gd1d4] }
( 5... Bg4 ) 6. Qxd4
