7. c3 ( 7. Re1 ) ( 7. a4 ) ( 7. d3 ) ( 7. Ng5 d5 8. exd5
{ White's premature knight raid against f7 has provoked [d5], shutting the a2 to g8 diagonal. Just as in the Two Knights Defence, Black must resist recapturing on d5 with the f6-knight and instead jump forward to [Nd4], hitting White's bishop on b3 and cutting its line to f7; after [Nd4 Re1 Bc5 Rxe5+ Kf8], Black's active minor pieces outweigh the sacrificed pawn. [%csl Yf7,Ya2,Yg8][%cal Gc6d4] }
