{ White opens the center before Black's bishop reaches g7. Black must capture with [exd4]: after [exd4 Nxd4 Bg7 Be3 Nge7], White enjoys extra central space and plans [w:Qd2], [w:O-O-O], and [w:f3] or [w:h4], while Black counterattacks d4 along the long diagonal and prepares [b:O-O] and [b:d5] (or [b:f5]). Trying to hold e5 with [b:Bg7] invites [w:Bg5] or [w:dxe5], while [d6] tangles Black's pieces. [%csl Gg7,Gd4,Ge5][%cal Ge5d4] }
