{ Black opens the e-file and challenges the knight. [Nxd4] is the standard recapture, reaching the Four Knights Scotch proper (see the Scotch Game chapter for [Nxd4 Bb4] and [Nxd4 Bc5]). [Nd5] is the Belgrade Gambit, introduced by Yugoslav masters in Belgrade around 1945, where White sacrifices the e4 pawn to plant an active knight on d5 and press down the half-open e-file. [%csl Ge4,Gd5][%cal Gf3d4] }
( 4... Bb4
