( 5. d5
{ The Closed Four Knights Scotch. White gains central space and kicks the c6 knight. Black should retreat calmly with [Ne7] (followed by [Ne7 Bd3 d6 O-O O-O] and [b:Ng6] plus a later [b:c6] or [b:f5] break) or trade first with [Bxc3+] [w:bxc3] [b:Ne7]. Jumping forward into d4 (the Oxford Gambit) drops material because no pawn supports d4 and e5 hangs. [%csl Gc6,Gd4,Ge5][%cal Gc6e7] }
