{ The Belgrade Gambit. Instead of recapturing on d4, White centralizes the queen's knight and offers the e4 pawn to open lines against Black's king. Black has three good ways to meet it: [Nb4] challenges the d5 outpost immediately (forcing [Nb4 Bc4] or [Nb4 Nxb4 Bxb4+]), [Be7] develops calmly and prepares to castle before touching e4, and [Nxe4] accepts the gambit as long as Black knows [Nxe4 Qe2 f5] (trading [b:Nxd5] [w:exd5] concedes space). [%csl Gd4,Ge4,Gd5][%cal Gc6b4] }
