{ The Glek System, championed since the late 1980s by GM Igor Glek. White fianchettoes on g2 to reinforce e4 and d5, keeping pieces on the board for a King's Indian Attack buildup with [w:Bg2], [w:d3], [w:O-O], and later [w:h3], [w:Nh4], and [w:f4]. Black has four playable replies: [d5] strikes in the center before the bishop reaches g2, [Bc5] claims the a7-g1 diagonal, [Bb4] pins c3, and the bold [Nxe4] ([Nxe4 Nxe4 d5 Nc3 d4 Ne2 e4 Nh4]) leads to an equal, double-edged fight. [%csl Gg2,Ge4,Gd5][%cal Gd7d5] }
