{ The Halloween Gambit, sacrificing a whole knight for a single pawn to chase Black's knights with [Nxe5 d4] and [w:e5]. It scores dangerously well in club blitz against passive defenders, yet against accurate play ([Nxe5 d4 Ng6], or [Nxe5 d4 Nc6] returning the piece with [b:Bb4]) Black consolidates with a clear advantage. Play [w:Bb5] or [w:d4] for a sound fight. [%cal Gc6e5] }
