{ White aims at f7 and prepares [w:Qf3]. The secret to beating the Halloween Gambit is never to sit passively a piece up: [d5]! gives back one pawn immediately to open the c8 bishop and stop White's steamroller cold ([d5 Bxd5 c6 Bb3 Bb4] or [d5 Bxd5 c6 Bb3 Be6], with a clear advantage for Black). [Bb4] pinning c3 first is strong too, whereas timid [b:d6] lets White build awkward pressure with [w:Qf3]. [%csl Gf7,Gc8,Gc3][%cal Gd7d5] }
( 7. Qf3 ) ( 7. f4 $2
