{ The Wayward Queen (or Parham) Attack, a beginner favorite aiming for Scholar's Mate and played in over thirty million online games. White hits e5 and eyes f7 at the cost of exposing the queen to minor-piece tempo hits. Black's textbook response is [Nc6], defending e5 while developing naturally so [Nc6 Bc4] can be met cleanly by [b:g6]. [Nf6] is the sharp Kiddie Countergambit ([Nf6 Qxe5+ Be7]), whereas [g6] one move too soon blunders the h8 rook. [%csl Ge5,Gf7,Gh8][%cal Gb8c6] }
