4. fxe5 Nxe4 5. Qg4 ) ) ( 3. f3 $2
{ Guarding e4 a second time with [w:f3] blocks g1, weakens the a7-g1 and e1-h4 diagonals, and lets [d5 Ne2 Bc5] clamp White's king in the center. Develop [w:Nf3] instead. [%csl Rf3,Ye1][%cal Gd7d5] }
3... d5 4. Ne2 Bc5 ) ( 3. Qf3 $6
{ Bringing the queen to f3 blocks the g1 knight's best square and exposes her to nasty knight leaps onto d4. Black strikes in the centre with [d5], and after [d5 Bg5 Nc6 exd5 Nd4] White's queen is driven right back to d1 with big loss of time. Develop [Nf3] or [Nc3] instead. [%csl Rf3,Yg1][%cal Gd7d5] }
3... d5 4. Bg5 Nc6 5. exd5 Nd4 ) ) 2... exd4 ( 2... Nf6 $2
