3. dxe5 Nxe4 4. Bc4
{ When Black meets the Center Game with [b:Nf6], [w:dxe5] [b:Nxe4] followed by developing the bishop to c4 puts immediate heat on f7 and prepares [w:Qd5] or [w:Qf3] double attacks against f7 and the loose e4 knight. Notice that [b:Bc5] blunders into [w:Qd5]; Black must play [c6], [Nc5], or [d6], or try the counterattack [Qh4], which White meets cleanly with [Qh4 Be3]. [%csl Gc4,Gf7,Ge4][%cal Gc7c6] }
4... c6 ( 4... Nc5 ) ( 4... d6 ) ( 4... Qh4
