{ Threatening mate on f7 catches careless players who push [d5], yet Black easily parries both threats with [Ng5] (or [Nf6]) and gains time on White's exposed queen. Pin along the e-file with [Qe2], where Black has no clean retreat. [%csl Rf7][%cal Ge4g5] }
4... Ng5 5. Qe3 Be7 ) ( 4. Nxf7 $4
{ The Cochrane-like fork on d8 and h8 walks straight into a devastating discovered-check trap! Instead of taking the knight, Black plays [Qe7], pinning the e-file; if White grabs [Qe7 Nxh8 Nc3+ Be2 Nxd1], Black wins White's queen for a rook and piece. Pin Black's own knight with [Qe2] or play [d4] instead. [%csl Rf7,Ye4][%cal Gd8e7] }
