{ Here lies the sting of the Kholmov Gambit: clinging stubbornly to the e5 pawn walks into sharp traps. White's cleanest antidote is to return the pawn on White's own terms with [Nc3], when [Nc3 Qxe5 Qxe5+ Nxe5 Bf4] gives a lasting bishop-pair initiative, or [Bb5] met by [Bd7] and [Nc3]. Trying to hold e5 with [Bf4] invites the thrust [b:g5], while [f4] loosens White's uncastled king. [%csl Ye5][%cal Gb1c3] }
