{ Attacking the knight on e5 with [Qe7] wins back e4, yet clogs Black's own f8 bishop behind the queen. White shouldn't retreat the knight yet. Instead, play [d4] first, seizing the centre and opening both bishops so that after [d4 d6 Nf3 Qxe4+ Be2] White castles quickly and hits the exposed queen with [Nc3] and [w:Re1]. Every tempo White gains chasing that exposed queen down the e-file translates directly into central control. [%csl Ye5,Ye4][%cal Gd2d4] }
