{ The Stafford Gambit, tried by Howard Staunton in 1857, named after Joseph Stafford's six-move 1950 correspondence win over Irving Lowens, and turned into an online blitz favourite by Eric Rosen, who beat Sergey Erenburg with it in 14 moves at the 2024 World Blitz. Accepting with [Nxc6] is White's objective refutation, while [d4] and [Nf3] decline safely if White prefers calm waters. [%cal Ge5c6] }
