{ White trades off Black's queenside knight and asks how Black recaptures on c6. The whole point of the Stafford Gambit is [dxc6], taking away from the corner so the queen's d-file and the c8 bishop's diagonal both spring open in one move toward f2 and g4. Recapturing with the b-pawn instead would leave Black's pieces boxed in with nothing to show for the sacrificed central pawn. [%csl Yc6,Yf2,Yg4][%cal Gd7c6] }
( 4. Nxf7 $4
{ Playing a Cochrane-style sacrifice here is unsound because Black already has [Nc6] developed and hasn't spent a tempo on [d6]. After [Kxf7 Bc4+ d5], Black shuts down the diagonal and consolidates the extra piece cleanly. Simply trade knights with [Nxc6]. [%cal Ge8f7] }
