5. Qe2 ) ) ( 4. Nf3
{ Retreating [Nf3] is the quiet 'Anti-Stafford' sidestep: White hands back the e4 pawn voluntarily to avoid sharp gambit memorization altogether, accepting a dead-even game. Black should capture immediately with [Nxe4], reaching a comfortable Classical or Four-Knights Petrov where Black's queenside knight is already developed on c6 for free. Although unambitious, it guarantees a calm, solid position for players who hate memorizing sharp gambit traps. [%csl Ye4,Yc6][%cal Gf6e4] }
