{ Black has regained the pawn with a free developing move on c6. White can steer into open play with [d4] (met by [d5], an improved Classical Petrov where [Bg4] and [Qf6] generate brisk pressure), challenge the knight Nimzowitsch-style with [Nc3] (met by solid [d5] or [b:Nxc3]), or trade queens via [Qe2] and [Qe7]. Black's extra tempo on c6 makes this one of the easiest positions in all [b:e5] openings for Black to play. [%csl Yc6][%cal Gd2d4] }
( 4... Bc5 $2
