6. h3
{ With [h3] on the board, [Ng4] is prevented and White still has the queen's diagonal open to meet [Qd4] with [Qf3], defending both f2 and e4 while offering a favourable queen trade. Black tries [Qd4], [O-O] or [Be6], while White follows calmly with [d3], [Be3] and [Qf3] or [Qe2] to castle queenside a clean pawn ahead. Once queens are traded or driven back, White's extra central pawn and clean structure decide the endgame. [%csl Yf2,Ye4][%cal Gd8d4] }
