{ A common club disaster: developing [Bc4] allows [Ng4], and castling [w:O-O] walks straight into [b:Qh4] [w:h3] [b:Nxf2] [w:Qf3] [b:Nxh3+] mating along the diagonal. Even [Ng4 Qf3 Ne5] hits both queen and bishop and gives Black the upper hand. Stop [Ng4] with [h3] first. [%cal Gf6g4] }
