f3
{ Ignore the beginner maxim 'never play f3'—against the Stafford Gambit, [f3] is a cold-blooded computer and grandmaster weapon. One quiet pawn move defends e4 and takes away g4 from Black's knight at the same time. Black's best tries are [Be6] (unpinning the e-file, where White answers [Qe2], not [c3]), [Bc5] (met by [c3] and [d4]) and tricky [Nh5] (met by [g3] stopping [Qh4+]). [%csl Ye4,Yg4][%cal Gc8e6] }
