{ Damiano's king hunt reaches its key junction. Black's only move to delay checkmate is [d5], sacrificing a pawn to deflect White's bishop: after [d5 Bxd5+ Kg6 h4], intending [w:h5+] and [w:d4+], [b:h6] gets mated by the deflection [Bxb7] [b:Bxb7] [Qf5+], and [b:h5] [Bxb7] [Bd6] [Qa5+] wins Black's c8-bishop and the game. [%cal Gd7d5] }
