{ The only fully sound Hanham fourth move against [Bc4]: [c6] covers d5 against [Qd5] and opens c7 and b6 for Black's queen so [Be7] becomes playable next turn. White usually castles [O-O] aiming for Steiner's [dxe5] bishop-pair squeeze, develops [Nc3] in Schlechter's line, plays [a4] to restrain [b5], or props up the centre with [c3]. Black's goal is to reach [b:Be7], [b:Ngf6] and [b:O-O] intact, then expand on the queenside with [b:b5] and [b:Qc7]. [%csl Yd5,Yc7,Yb6][%cal Ge1g1] }
