{ Striking in the centre with [d4] forces Black's hand and opens the c1-bishop's diagonal before Black's kingside pieces come out. Black must push [e4] to keep lines closed and chase White's f3-knight, because trading [b:exd4] [w:Qxd4] [b:Nf6] [w:Bg5] leaves White a clean pawn ahead with open central files and rapid queenside castling. After [e4], White's knight jumps forward to e5 rather than retreating, locking down the centre a full pawn ahead. [%csl Ye5][%cal Ge5e4] }
