[Event "Vienna Game and Bishop's Opening (1)"]

{ Lichess Neo's coach explains these positions in its Game Review. In a comment, [Nf3] is a move, [Qb3 Qxb3 axb3] moves one after the other, [w:Re1] a later move of White, and a square is written as it is, e5. Each position's first moves are those theory goes on with. }
1. e4 e5 2. Nc3
{ The Vienna Game, named after Carl Hamppe of Vienna and championed by Steinitz, Spielmann and Larsen. Developing the queen's knight before [Nf3] guards e4 and controls d5 while keeping White's f-pawn unblocked to launch an improved King's Gambit with [w:f4]. Black's two principled replies are [Nf6] (the Falkbeer Variation, attacking e4 to prepare [b:d5] against [w:f4]) and [Nc6] (the Max Lange Defense, holding d4 and e5); [Bc5], [Bb4] and [d6] are playable sidelines. [%csl Ge4,Gd5,Gd4,Ge5][%cal Gg8f6] }
( 2. Bc4
{ The Bishop's Opening, analysed by Ruy Lopez in 1561, championed by Philidor and Larsen, and used by Kasparov, Carlsen and Duda to sidestep Petrov and Ruy Lopez theory on move two. Developing the bishop first eyes f7, keeps the f-pawn unblocked for [w:f4] and prepares [w:c3] plus [w:d4] or the Urusov Gambit. Black's main replies are [Nf6], [Bc5], [Nc6] and [c6]. [%csl Gf7][%cal Gg8f6] }
2... Nf6
{ The Berlin Defense is Black's sharpest and most popular answer to the Bishop's Opening: attacking e4 on move two forces White to declare an intention immediately. White chooses between the solid [d3] (Quiet Berlin), the sharp Urusov Gambit [d4], [Nc3] (Stanley and Vienna Hybrid), and [Nf3] (Petrov and Boden-Kieseritzky). Avoid passive [f3 d5], premature [f4 Nxe4], and [Ne2 Nxe4]. [%csl Ge4][%cal Gd2d3] }
( 2... Bc5
{ The Classical (Boi) Defense mirrors White's bishop to eye f2 and control d4. White has five sound plans: [Nf3] (entering the Giuoco Piano after [Nf3 Nc6]), Philidor's [c3] (preparing [w:d4] immediately while Black lacks [Nc6]), [Nc3] (setting up the Copycat attack if Black plays [b:Nc6]), Lopez's [Qe2], and quiet [d3]. Gambits like [d4] (Lewis), [b4] (Wing) and early [Qg4] are sharp sidelines. [%csl Gf2,Gd4][%cal Gg1f3] }
