{ The Steinitz Gambit, introduced by Wilhelm Steinitz in 1867 and occasionally used in rapid play by Carlsen: White claims the full centre on move four and invites Black to displace White's king. Black must test the idea with [Qh4+] ([Ke2]); timid replies like [g5 h4], [d6 Bxf4] or [Nf6 e5] miss the one moment h4 was open and leave White castling normally with a dominant centre. [%csl Gh4][%cal Gd8h4] }
