{ The Vienna Hybrid, reached from [Nc3] [Nc6] [Bc4] [Nf6], [Nc3] [Nf6] [Bc4] [Nc6] and the Bishop's Opening [Bc4] [Nf6] [Nc3] [Nc6]. White's key move is [d3], keeping the g1-knight at home for one turn so the f-pawn stays free to launch Spielmann's [w:f4] attack ([Nf3] enters the Four Knights Italian). Pushing [f4] before [d3] walks straight into the centre-fork trick [f4 Nxe4]. [%cal Gd2d3] }
