{ White refuses to release the central tension, so Black captures [dxe5] to open the d-file toward White's queen on d1 and prevent [w:Bxf4] from arriving unchallenged. That capture sets one final trap on h4: if White recaptures carelessly with the f3-knight, Black fires [b:Qh4+] along the reopened diagonal. Instead of recapturing with knight or pawn on the next move, White pins the e5-pawn with [w:Qe2] to keep maximum pressure on Black's centre. [%csl Gd1,Gh4][%cal Gd6e5] }
( 6. exd6 $6
{ Trading on d6 helps Black bring out [Bxd6], anchoring f4 while clearing the back rank for [Nf6] and [O-O]. Keep tension and build the centre with [d4]. [%csl Rd6,Rf4][%cal Rf8d6] }
