{ Black blockades White's e5-pawn and reinforces d5 with the light-squared bishop on e6. White develops [Bf4], controlling e5 while clearing the queenside back rank so [w:O-O-O] places White's rook on d1 directly opposite Black's d5-pawn and queen on d8, setting up central pin motifs if Black develops the b8-knight carelessly. Once [Bf4 c5 O-O-O] is on the board, Black must develop the b8-knight to d7 rather than c6 so [w:Bc4] never wins the pinned d5-pawn. [%csl Gd5,Ge6,Ge5,Gd1][%cal Gc1f4] }
