7... c5
{ Black stakes out queenside space with [c5] and prepares [b:Qb6] or [b:Qa5]. White castles long with [O-O-O], bringing the rook onto d1 directly opposite Black's d5-pawn and queen on d8. That x-ray down the d-file forces Black to choose the right square for the queen's knight on the very next turn. Watch that d-file alignment on the next move: if Black develops [O-O-O Nc6], White's [w:Bc4] piles three pieces onto d5 and wins a pawn. [%csl Gd1,Gd8,Gd5][%cal Ge1c1] }
( 7... Nd7 ) 8. O-O-O
