{ Against Bardeleben's 5.[f5], White refuses [w:exf6] [b:Nxf6] and attacks the e4-knight at its base with [d3]. Because any knight retreat to c5 or g5 drops the central d5-pawn with tempo to [w:Qxd5], Black is practically forced to trade knights on c3 with [Nxc3] ([w:bxc3]) and push [b:d4] immediately before White builds a broad pawn centre. Once [Nxc3 bxc3] lands, Black must push [b:d4] right away to stop White from playing [w:d4] and dominating the whole board. [%csl Gc5,Gg5,Gc3][%cal Ge4c3] }
