{ Black accepts the c3-pawn bait, opening lines on the queenside while the king still sits in the middle of the board with f5 advanced. White calmly develops [Be2], aiming straight down the weakened e2-h5 diagonal so that any routine developing move from Black runs into a devastating bishop sacrifice on h5 and g6. If Black carelessly develops [Be2 Nc6] on the next move, [w:Bh5+] [b:g6] [w:Bxg6+] rips Black's kingside shelter to pieces. [%csl Gf5,Ge2,Gh5,Gg6][%cal Gf1e2] }
9. Be2
{ Watch the e2-h5 diagonal: White threatens [w:Bh5+] [b:g6] [w:Bxg6+] [b:hxg6] [w:Qxg6+], tearing open Black's uncastled king. Black must cover h5 and g6 immediately with [Be6] or [g6] ([Bf3 Nc6 Ne2]). Developing [Nc6] on autopilot gets crushed by force after [Nc6 Bh5+ g6 Bxg6+ hxg6 Qxg6+], winning the queen if [b:Ke7] [w:Bg5+]. [%csl Ge2,Gh5,Gg6][%cal Gc8e6] }
