{ White's pawn on g3 blocks the check and attacks Black's queen on h4. Black has no real choice now but to capture [fxg3], since retreating the queen would drop both g4 and f4 for nothing while leaving White's knights dominating the middle of the board. The real test arrives one move later when White captures on g4. After [fxg3 Qxg4], Black must trade queens on g4 and strike with [b:d5] rather than grab the h1-rook via [b:g2+] and get mated on f7. [%csl Gg3,Gh4,Gg4,Gf4][%cal Gf4g3] }
