3... d5 4. Bxd5 Nf6 ) 3... d6
{ The main tabiya of the Classical King's Gambit Declined. Black's bishop on c5 prevents White from castling short because g1 sits under fire along the a7-g1 diagonal. White's sharpest modern plan is Marshall's [c3], preparing [w:d4] to shut the diagonal down with tempo and unlock short castling; [Nc3] and [Bc4] aim to trade off the c5-bishop via [w:Na4] or [w:Be3], while [fxe5] ([dxe5]) opens the f-file early. Because castling short is illegal while Black's bishop rakes g1, every sound White plan either blocks the diagonal with [c3] and [w:d4] or trades off the bishop via [Nc3] and [w:Na4]. [%csl Gc5,Gg1,Ga7][%cal Gc2c3] }
( 3... exf4 $2
