{ The Sveshnikov. Black hits the knight and claims the centre, accepting a hole on d5 and a backward pawn on d6 in exchange for activity and fast development. It became a top-level weapon thanks to Kramnik and Carlsen. White's best is [Ndb5], which eyes d6, so Black has to answer [d6] at once. The other retreats are tame: after [Nb3] or [Nf3], the bishop comes to b4 and pins the knight on c3, and [Nf5] runs into [d5]. [%csl Rd5,Rd6][%cal Gd4b5] }
