{ The Westerinen Attack prepares to fianchetto the queen's bishop to b2 to back up e4 and aim through the centre toward g7. Because White holds back [d4], Black gets easy equality in several ways: [d5] challenges e4 right away ([d5 exd5 exd5 Bb5+ Bd7]), while [Nc6] and [a6] prepare [b:d5] or [b:Nf6] without letting White pin the knight. White follows up with [Bb2], [Bd3] or [Bb5], and short castling. [%cal Gb8c6,Gd7d5,Bc1b2] }
