{ The Deferred Wing Gambit sacrifices a flank pawn to deflect Black's c-pawn away from d4 so White can build a broad centre. Accepting with [cxb4] is critical: White continues [cxb4 a3] (when [b:bxa3] [w:Nxa3] or [b:d5] [w:exd5] [b:exd5] gives balanced play) or [cxb4 d4] [b:d5] [w:e5], reaching an Advance French structure where Black holds an extra queenside pawn. [b6] declines solidly and keeps tension. [%csl Yd4][%cal Gc5b4,Gb7b6] }
