{ The Kramnik Variation. White clamps d5 before playing [d4], often with [Nc3] and [d4] later, or keeps the game closed with [d3] and [g3]. Black has an easy game: [Nc6] with [Nf6], [d6] and [Be7], or a Hedgehog with [a6], [b6] and [Bb7], keeping the breaks [b5] and [d5] in reserve. The hole on d4 is the price of [c4]: a black knight that gets there is very strong. [%csl Yd5,Rd4][%cal Gb8c6,Ga7a6] }
3... Nc6 ( 3... a6
{ Black sets up a Kan-Hedgehog shell against the Kramnik [c4] system, taking b5 away from White's pieces and preparing [b:Qc7], [b:b6] and [b:Bb7]. [Nc3] keeps tension and stops [b:b5], often followed by [Be2], [O-O] and [d4] once White is fully castled, whereas [d4] immediately enters the Paulsen Maroczy Bind ([d4 cxd4 Nxd4]), where Black undermines the c4-e4 clamp later with [b:b5] or [b:d5]. [%csl Yd5][%cal Gb1c3,Gd2d4] }
4. Nc3 ( 4. d4 ) ) ) ) ( 2... g6
{ The Hyper-Accelerated Dragon. Black prepares to put the bishop on g7 before committing the queen's knight or the d-pawn. After [d4 cxd4 Nxd4], the knight move [Nc6] reaches the Accelerated Dragon. White has alternatives that use the move order: [c3], aiming for [d4] with a pawn recapture, meets the bishop with a solid chain; [c4] sets up a Maroczy Bind at once; and [d4 cxd4 Qxd4] hits the rook on h8. If White plays [d4 Bg7 dxc5], Black wins the pawn back with [Qa5]. [%cal Gd2d4,Gc2c3,Gc2c4,Bf8g7] }
3. d4
{ White opens the centre against the Hyper-Accelerated Dragon. [cxd4] is the main move: after [cxd4 Nxd4 Nc6] the game is an Accelerated Dragon, and [cxd4 Qxd4] hits the rook on h8, so Black blocks with [Nf6]. [Bg7] keeps the tension and invites [dxc5], which Black meets with [Qa5+] and wins the pawn back. With [Bg7], though, White can also play [d5] or [c3] for a big centre, so most players simply take. [%csl Yd4][%cal Gc5d4,Gf8g7] }
( 3. c3
{ White prepares [d4], so that the c-pawn can take back and keep two pawns in the centre. Black's most natural move is [Bg7], aiming at d4 along the long diagonal; after [d4 cxd4 cxd4 d5], Black hits the centre at once. [d5] straight away is also good: after [d5 exd5 Qxd5 d4], the queen stands in the centre as in the Alapin, and the bishop goes to g7 to add pressure on d4. [%csl Yd4][%cal Gf8g7,Gd7d5] }
