{ Against White's Alapin [c3], Black calmly completes the fianchetto with [Bg7] instead of striking immediately with [d5]. That invites White to claim the full pawn center with [d4], after which [d4 cxd4 cxd4 d5] hits e4 and d4 at the exact moment White's pawns step forward: [d4 cxd4 cxd4 d5 exd5 Nf6] leads to an active Grünfeld-like IQP battle where Black's g7-bishop shines against d4, while [d4 cxd4 cxd4 d5 e5 Bg4] locks in White's center and targets f3 and d4. [%cal Gd2d4,Bg7d4] }
