{ Black picks the move order. [Nc6] reaches the Accelerated Dragon. [Bg7] hits the knight on d4 at once and keeps [Nc6] in reserve; White usually answers with [c4] or [Nc3]. [Nf6] attacks e4 and asks for [Nc3], after which Black must still cover e5 with [Nc6] or [d6], or the push [e5] kicks the knight. In every version the fianchettoed bishop is Black's best piece, so Black should trade it only for a good reason. [%cal Gf8g7,Gb8c6,Gg8f6] }
( 4. Qxd4
{ Chekhover's queen recapture against the Hyper-Accelerated Dragon. Because Black has not yet played [Bg7], White's queen on d4 directly attacks the undefended rook on h8 along the long diagonal and forces Black's hand. Black blocks with [Nf6], developing while preparing [Nc6] to gain time on the queen, and after [Nf6 e5 Nc6 Qa4 Nd5] reaches an unbalanced, dynamic struggle where White's space contends with Black's active minor pieces. [%cal Gg8f6,Rd4h8,Gb8c6] }
