{ The Hyper-Accelerated Dragon tabiya. Black's bishop is already raking d4 from g7, while both knights stay flexible at home. White's most testing try is [c4], establishing the Maroczy Bind on c4 and e4 before [b:Nc6] or [d5] can challenge the centre; Black then plays [b:Nc6] into the main Maroczy lines or [Qa5+] to disrupt coordination. [Nc3] and [Be3] keep piece play lively and transpose to the Accelerated Dragon after [b:Nc6]. [%cal Gc2c4,Gb1c3,Gc1e3,Gg7d4] }
( 4... Nc6 ) ( 4... Nf6
{ The knight hits e4, and White must guard it with [Nc3]: the bishop move and the pawn push both lose a pawn here. After [Nc3], Black chooses between [Nc6], an Accelerated Dragon, and [d6], a normal Dragon, and should not play [Bg7] first, since [e5] would kick the knight back to g8. The fianchettoed bishop is coming anyway; covering e5 comes first. [%csl Ye5][%cal Gb1c3,Rf6e4] }
