( 4. c3
{ White offers a Morra-style pawn against the O'Kelly. Black's best is to take it with [dxc3]: after [dxc3 Nxc3], White has a Morra in which Black's [b:a6] is already useful, as it keeps the knight off b5. [Nf6] hits e4 at once and is also good. Holding the pawn with the e-pawn fails to [w:Nxe5], and a waiting move simply lets White take back with the c-pawn and keep a big centre for nothing. [%csl Ye4][%cal Gd4c3,Gg8f6] }
