{ The Zagorovsky Line against the O'Kelly Variation ([a6]). Because [w:Nxd4] would walk straight into [b:e5] (with b5 already taken away by a6) or [b:e6] and [b:Qc7], White recaptures with the queen via [Qxd4]! However, a6 actually helps Black here too: since [Nc6] can no longer be met by [Bb5], Black chases the queen cleanly with [Nc6] (forcing [Nc6 Qd1], [Nc6 Qd2] or [Nc6 Qe3]) and gains smooth development with [Nf6] and [d6] or [e6]. [%cal Gb8c6,Ge7e6,Rc6d4] }
