{ The Cortlever Gambit against the O'Kelly: White leaves the d4-pawn untouched for a moment to aim the bishop at f7 and invite tactical slips. Black neutralizes the trick effortlessly with [e6], blunting the a2-g8 diagonal so White has nothing better than [e6 Nxd4] into a comfortable Kan structure, or [Nf6] hitting e4 right back. Clinging to the extra pawn with [e5] weakens d5 and f7 and walks into [e5 c3]. [%csl Yf7][%cal Ge7e6,Gg8f6] }
4... e6 ( 4... Nf6 ) ( 4... e5 $6
