{ Here is the direct point of the O'Kelly [a6]: Black kicks the d4-knight with [e5] while b5 is already covered, claiming central space even though d5 becomes weak and the d7-pawn stays behind. [Nb3] and [Nf3] are White's best retreats — from f3 the knight hits e5 at once ([Nf3 Nf6 Bc4]), while from b3 it leaves the f-pawn free and eyes a5 and c5 as White prepares [Nc3] and [Be3] or [Bg5]. [%csl Yd5][%cal Gd4b3,Gd4f3] }
