{ The pure Classical Scheveningen tabiya. Both kings have castled short, and Black's [Nc6] adds heat to d4 while opening the door for [Qb6] along the a7-g1 diagonal. White's top priority is securing that diagonal with either [Be3]—bolstering d4 and getting ready for [Qe1] and [Qg3]—or the prophylactic [Kh1]. Impatient pawn breaks like [e5] or [f5] backfire at once because [Qb6] pins the d4-knight to White's king. [%cal Gc1e3,Gg1h1,Rc6d4] }
