{ The Fischer-Sozin Attack aims the bishop down the a2-g8 diagonal at e6 and f7, preparing [Bb3], [Be3] (or [O-O]) and a timely [f4]-[f5] pawn battering ram to pry open Black's centre. Black answers with [a6] — preparing [b:b5] with tempo on the bishop and entering Najdorf Sozin territory — or [Be7] and [Nc6], completing kingside development before counterattacking down the half-open c-file. [%csl Yf7][%cal Ga7a6,Gf8e7,Gb8c6] }
