{ White opens the centre at once. Black's best is to take, and White then chooses how to go on. [c3] offers a pawn: the Smith-Morra Gambit. [Nf3] develops first and usually returns to an Open Sicilian. Taking back with the queen is possible, but after [cxd4 Qxd4 Nc6] the queen is chased. Not taking lets White's d-pawn take space or the pawn on c5. [%csl Yd4,Ye4][%cal Gc5d4] }
2... cxd4
{ White has to decide what to do about the pawn on d4. [c3] is the Smith-Morra Gambit: a pawn for fast development and two open files. [Nf3] develops first, and the knight takes on d4 next move. [Qxd4] takes at once, but the queen is hit by [Nc6] and White loses time. [%cal Gc2c3,Gg1f3,Gd1d4] }
( 2... Nc6 $2
