{ The knight develops to its natural square, adds a second guard to d4 and keeps the push to e5 in reserve. White's main move is [d4], the Open Sicilian, after which Black can choose the Sveshnikov, the Accelerated Dragon, the Kalashnikov or the Taimanov. [Bb5], the Rossolimo, is the most respected way to avoid all that. [Nc3] keeps the options open, [c3] is an Alapin with the knight already out, and [Bc4] is a common club move. [%cal Gd2d4,Gf1b5,Gb1c3] }
