( 3. Bb5
{ The Rossolimo Variation, the most respected way to avoid the Open Sicilian after [Nc6]. The bishop puts pressure on the knight that controls d4 and e5, and White is often happy to take on c6, doubling Black's pawns and playing against them later. Black's main answers are [g6], putting the bishop on the long diagonal; [e6], preparing [Nge7] so that a capture on c6 can be met by the knight; and [d6], which reaches the Moscow Variation's position with the knight on c6. [%csl Yc6][%cal Gg7g6,Ge7e6,Gd7d6] }
