( 3... e6
{ Black prepares [Nge7], so that a capture on c6 can be met by the knight and the pawns stay healthy. The pawn on e6 also gets ready for [d5], Black's natural central break. White usually castles and plays [Re1], and if Black chases the bishop with [a6], it often drops back to f1, where it still supports the center. [Bxc6] at once, followed by [d3] and [b3], plays against the doubled pawns before Black can avoid them. [%csl Yg8,Ye7][%cal Ge1g1,Gb5c6] }
