{ The Adams Attack, a modern favourite. The modest pawn on h3 prepares [g4], a pawn storm that chases the knight from f6, and it also takes g4 away from Black's knight, so a bishop on e3 can't be harassed. Black's most common answer is [e5], after which the knight retreats to e2 or b3 and [g4] still comes. Against [e6], the push [g4] recalls the Keres Attack, and Black often hits back with [d5] while White's king is still on e1. [%cal Gh3h4,Gg2g4] }
