dxc3 4. Nxc3 Nc6
{ Black develops the knight to its best square. White goes on with the standard Morra set-up: [Nf3], [Bc4], castling, [Qe2] and the rooks to d1 and c1; the order of [Nf3] and [Bc4] hardly matters. The key squares are d6, where a knight from b5 or a rook on the d-file can land, and f7, which the bishop on c4 watches. Black's job is to finish development without handing the pawn back too soon, with [d6], [e6] and [Nf6], or [e6], [a6] and [Nge7]. [%csl Yd6,Yf7][%cal Gg1f3,Gf1c4] }
