{ Black's set-up with [d6] keeps e5 covered. White plays [Bc4], castling, [Qe2] and the rooks to d1 and c1. Black must watch f7: the bishop on c4 and a knight jump to g5 aim at it. The two classic errors come right after [Bc4]: [Bg4], which loses to [Bxf7+] and [Ng5], and, after [Bc4 Nf6 e5], the capture on e5, which runs into a combination on f7. Black's safe plan is [e6], [Nf6], [Be7] and castling, or [a6] first. [%csl Yf7,Yd5][%cal Gf1c4] }
