{ The Pin Defense develops Black's dark-squared bishop actively to b4, clearing the kingside for [b:Nge7] and [b:O-O] while threatening to double White's c-pawns. Castling with [O-O] is White's sharpest reply: if Black grabs [O-O Bxc3 bxc3], White's dark-squared bishop rakes the board from a3 to prevent castling, and after [O-O Nge7], [w:Qe2] and [w:Rd1] (or [w:Nb5]) keep strong central pressure. [Bd2] unpins quietly. [%csl Yb4][%cal Ge1g1,Gc1d2] }
