{ In the Smith-Morra Gambit, Black develops [Bc5] actively outside the e6-pawn chain—controlling the a7-g1 diagonal and eyeing f2—instead of tucking the bishop passively on e7. The catch is that [Bc5] leaves g7 unguarded and stands exposed to [Qe2] + [Be3] trades or [Bg5] pins (since e7 has no bishop!). White usually plays [O-O] and [Qe2] followed by [w:Rd1] and [Bf4] or [Bg5], forcing Black to play [Nge7] accurately rather than walking into [b:Nf6] met by [e5]. [%cal Gd1e2,Gc1f4,Gc1g5] }
