{ The Classical / Najdorf-style Defense to the Smith-Morra Gambit. Black has prevented [Nb5] with [a6], guarded e5 with [d6], and now develops [Nf6]—hitting White's e4-pawn while threatening [Bg4] to pin the f3-knight and fight for d4! White has three thematic responses: [Qe2] defends e4 while preparing [Rd1] (where [Qe2 Bg4 Rd1] dares Black to enter tactical fire on d5 and f7), [h3] stops [Bg4] cold before [Qe2] and [Be3], while [Bf4] pressures d6 and [e5] rips open central lines. [%cal Gd1e2,Gh2h3,Rf6e4] }
