{ With knights opposing each other on the c-file, the battle revolves around the central outposts d5 and d4. White controls d5 with two pawns and a knight, while Black eyes the backward-pawn hole on d4 and prepares [g6] and [Bg7] so the fianchettoed bishop adds maximum pressure down the long diagonal. White usually continues with [g3] and [Bg2] for a reversed Botvinnik English structure, or [Nf3] and [d4] to open the center right away before Black's bishop reaches g7. [%csl Yd4,Gd5][%cal Gg2g3,Gg1f3] }
