{ The Gurgenidze Variation of the Accelerated Dragon Maroczy Bind: Black has traded knights on d4 so the two minor-piece pairs won't trip over each other inside Black's cramped three-rank camp, even though bringing White's queen to d4 costs a tempo. [d6] is mandatory right here to stop [w:e5] from kicking the f6-knight back to g8. Afterward, Black finishes with [b:Bg7], [b:O-O] and [b:Be6] — challenging White's queen and the c4-pawn — followed by [b:Nd7] and [b:a5] to anchor a knight on c5 while White builds methodically with [w:Be2], [w:Be3], [w:Qd2] and [w:O-O]. [%csl Ye5,Yc5][%cal Gd7d6] }
