{ White trades knights before Black has played [Bg7]. Black takes back toward the centre with [bxc6]: the pawn on c6 supports [d5], and the b-file opens for a rook. [dxc6] offers a queen trade that leaves the king in the centre, though the endgame is about level. White's most testing idea is [Qd4], hitting the rook on h8 through the empty g7 square: Black blocks with [Nf6] and gets the bishop to g7 soon after. [%cal Gb7c6,Gd7c6,Bd7d5] }
