{ The Dragon. The bishop goes to g7, where it sweeps the long diagonal toward d4 and the queenside and becomes Black's best piece. Black castles short and plays on the c-file, often giving the exchange on c3 to wreck White's queenside. The pawn chain on d6, e7, f7, g6 and h7 gave the line its name, and it has no weak pawn at all: e7 sits far back, out of reach, so the endgames tend to favour Black. White's sharpest answer is the Yugoslav Attack: [Be3], [f3], [Qd2], long castling and a storm with [h4] and [Bh6]. [Be2] with short castling is the calmer Classical Dragon, and [f4] sets a trap or two. [%csl Rc3][%cal Gf8g7,Bg7b2] }
