8. Be3 ) ( 7... Qh5 $4
{ The queen keeps the pin, but [d5] hits the knight on c6 and the queen on h5 does nothing about it. White wins material. [%csl Rc6][%cal Gd4d5] }
8. d5 ) 8. gxf3
{ White's pawn recapture on f3 removes the knight's guard over d4 while opening the g-file for White's rook. Black must follow through on the plan with [Qxd4], grabbing the central pawn and inviting [Qxd4 Qxd4 Nxd4]—where White answers [Nb5] or [Bb5] for active endgame play. Retreating the queen without taking d4 lets [d5] crush c6. [%csl Yd4,Yg1][%cal Gd5d4] }
