{ White prepares [d4], so that a trade on d4 can be met by the c-pawn and White keeps two pawns in the centre. With the pawn already on d6, Black's best answer is [Nf6], hitting e4 at once, and [g6] is also sound. [Nc6], the most natural-looking move, lets White carry out the plan: [d4] with the full centre. [d5] now would spend a second move on the d-pawn. [%cal Gg8f6,Gg7g6,Rf6e4] }
