{ The Richter-Rauzer Attack. The bishop eyes the knight on f6 and keeps Black from playing [g6]. White's plan is [Qd2] and long castling, then a pawn storm or pressure on d6 down the d-file. Black's main reply is [e6], followed by [a6] or the bishop to e7, and [Bd7] is the main alternative. In every line the knight jump to b5 against d6 is the danger to keep in mind. [%cal Gg5f6,Ge7e6,Gc8d7] }
