{ In the Richter-Rauzer main line, [e6] guards d5 and opens the f8-bishop's diagonal while accepting that [w:Bxf6] could double Black's f-pawns. [Qd2] is overwhelmingly the main continuation, preparing [O-O-O] to pile direct rook and queen pressure onto the backward d6-pawn against [b:a6] or [b:Be7] and [b:Bd7]. [Bb5] is a tricky sideline pinning the c6-knight ([Bb5 Bd7]) to intensify central pressure right away before Black castles. [%csl Yd6][%cal Gd1d2,Gf1b5] }
