5. b3 ) ) ( 4. dxc5 ) 4... exd5
{ [Ngf3] and [Bb5+] are the main moves. White's plan is to take on c5 when the bishop has moved, to win a tempo, and then blockade the isolated pawn with Nb3-d4. [dxc5] at once lets the bishop take back with development. Black's pieces get free development: ...Nf6, ...Nc6, ...Bd6, ...O-O and ...Re8 or ...Bg4. The isolated pawn on d5 needs care in the endgame. [%csl Yd5][%cal Gg1f3] }
( 4... Qxd5
