{ The fully symmetrical tabiya. [Bg5] pins the knight; Black copies with ...Bg4, and both sides bring the queen's knight to d7 or d2, the c-pawn to c6 or c3, and the queen to c7 or c2 with pressure on the kingside. Other plans are [h3] to keep the bishop out of g4 and [Re1] to take the open file. Black should not trade on f3 too early: White's queen would come to f3 with pressure on d5. [%csl Yd7,Yd5][%cal Gc1g5] }
