( 4... Bf5 $2
{ The bishop avoids the trade, but now nothing wins back d5. [c4] holds the pawn with a second one, and White is a clean pawn up with a good centre. The point of ...Bg4 against Be2 is to trade bishops and take on d5 with the queen, hitting g2. Play ...Bxe2 at once. [%csl Yd5][%cal Rc2c4,Be2g4] }
