4. dxe6 ) 4. Bc4 ( 4. Nf3 ) ( 4. d4 ) ( 4. Nxd5
{ White trades knights on d5, solving Black's opening problems at a stroke. [Qxd5] places the queen safely in the centre where no c3 knight remains to gain a tempo on her, while she eyes both g2 and a2 simultaneously. Black follows up smoothly with ...Nc6, ...Bg4 or ...Bf5, and ...O-O-O or ...e5, reaching an active, comfortable game with zero structural weaknesses. [%cal Gd8d5,Yd5g2,Yd5a2] }
4... Qxd5
{ Black's queen sits in the centre and eyes a2 and g2. [Nf3] is the engine's choice: it develops and guards g2, and Black can pin with ...Bg4 and castle long. [d4] takes the centre; Black answers with ...Bg4, ...Nc6 or ...e5. Black's plan: ...Nc6, ...Bg4 or ...Bf5, and ...O-O-O, with pressure on the d-file. With no knight on c3, White has no easy way to gain time on the queen, and a careless Be2 drops g2. [%csl Ye5,Yd7,Yd6][%cal Gd8d5] }
5. Nf3 ( 5. d4 ) ( 5. Be2 $2
