5... Qxg2 ) ) ) ( 3. Nf3
{ White develops the king's knight first, returning the d5 pawn cleanly without committing the c- or d-pawn early. [Nxd5] is the main recapture, usually transposing into the Modern lines once White follows with d4 and c4. [Bg4] pins f3 before recapturing on d5, and [Qxd5] enters a 2...Qxd5 3.Nf3 Nf6 position where White still holds Nc3 or c4 in reserve. [%cal Gf6d5,Gc8g4,Bd8d5] }
