5. d4
{ White has the centre. [c5] hits d4 at once and is the engine's choice: after c4, the knight goes to f6 or b4, and if d5, ...e6 hits the pawn. [Bf5] is the older move: the bishop gets a better diagonal, and White keeps a small edge with Nf3, O-O and c4. Passive set-ups let White grip the centre with c3 and Nbd2. [%csl Yc5][%cal Gc7c5] }
( 5. Nf3 ) 5... c5
{ Black hits d4. [c4] kicks the knight and builds a pawn duo; after ...Nf6, d5 and ...e6 lead to a sharp fight for the centre. [Nf3] develops; after ...cxd4 Nxd4 the game is open. [dxc5] wins a pawn for a moment but allows ...Qa5+ or ...e6 with quick development. White's pawn on d5 can be strong when it gains time. [%cal Gc2c4,Gg1f3,Bd4c5] }
( 5... Bf5 ) 6. c4
