{ The Boehnke gambit. Black gives the pawn to open lines for the light bishop. [dxe6] takes it en passant, and after ...Bxe6 Black has a lead in development and a free game, but a pawn is still a pawn. [c4] keeps the pawn on d5 with support; Black's ...Bd6 and ...Nf6 give some play. [Nc3] is also good. In all lines White simply develops and is better; Black's hope is that White falls behind in development trying to keep the pawn. [%cal Gd5e6,Gc2c4,Bb1c3] }
