{ White takes the centre and leaves Nc3 for later. [Nf6] is the main move: after Nf3 or Nc3 the game usually transposes to known lines. [e5] hits back at once, opening the game while White's king is still in the centre. ...Nc6, the engine's choice, leads to the Nimzowitsch Defence, an opening of its own. Developing the bishop to f5 first lets c4 and Nc3 gain time on the queen. White's idea here is c4, which kicks the queen with no knight in front of the c-pawn. [%cal Gg8f6,Be7e5,Gc2c4] }
3... Nf6 ( 3... e5
