( 5. d4 ) 5... Qc7 ( 5... Qa5 ) ) ( 3... Qe6+
{ A check that is very common in club games. The queen blocks Black's e-pawn and the bishop on f8, and will be hit again. [Be2] is the simplest: White follows with d4, Nf3 and O-O, and gains more time with d5 or Nb5 if the queen stays in the centre. [Nge2] blocks with the knight, heading for f4 or g3. Blocking with the queen offers a trade and gives most of the lead back. Black does best to bring the queen back to d7 or d6 soon and develop the knights. [%csl Ye6][%cal Gf1e2,Bg1e2] }
4. Be2
