{ White develops the knight before deciding between d4 and d3. [Nf6] and [c6] are the engine's choices: after d4 the main line is reached, and ...c6 also prepares the retreat to c7. Pinning at once with ...Bg4 is playable but h3 asks the bishop a question early. A useful thing to know: with the knight on f3 and no pawn on d4, White can play b4, gambiting a pawn to open the b-file against the queen. [%cal Gg8f6,Gc7c6,Bb2b4] }
