5. Qxg4 ) 5. d4 ( 5. Nf3 ) ( 5. d3 ) ) ( 4. g3
{ The fianchetto system. White plans Bg2, Nge2 and d3, then a quick b4-b5 against Black's queen and queenside; the bishop on g2 aims at b7. [Nf6] develops, and ...c6 follows. [e5] and [Nc6] take the centre at once, which the engine likes: White's d-pawn has not moved, so Black gets ...Nd4 and a share of the centre. Black should watch b7 and avoid putting the queen where b4 or Bd2 and Nd5 can hit her. [%csl Yg3,Yh3,Yd3][%cal Gg2g3] }
