{ White plays a modest centre and keeps the d-pawn out of reach. Black develops normally: [Nf6] and a bishop to f5 or g4. [g6] is the engine's choice: the bishop on g7 eyes b2 and the knight on c3. [e5] takes the centre at once, which is possible because White's pieces do not hit e5 yet. White's plan is often Bd2, Qe2, Nf3 and castling long, or a fianchetto with g3 and Bg2. Black's queen on a5 should be ready to retreat to c7 once a bishop reaches d2. [%cal Gg8f6,Gg7g6,Be7e5] }
