{ White aims a second piece at f7 and sets a venomous trap. [Nf6] is Black's best defence: the knight covers h5 and develops with tempo on e4. [e6] blunts the bishop at once, and Nc6 also guards the queen on a5. Kicking the knight with ...c6 or ...a6 is the mistake: Bxf7+ forces ...Kd8 with an ugly king, because taking on f7 loses Black's queen to Qh5+, ...g6 and Nd6+. [%csl Yh5,Yf7][%cal Gg8f6] }
