{ The Austrian Attack is White's most direct attempt to refute the Pirc: three pawns abreast seize central and kingside space, preparing either [w:e5] to spearhead an attack or [w:f5] to rip open the g-file. Black completes the fianchetto with [Bg7], putting immediate x-ray pressure on d4 and getting ready to castle or strike with [b:c5]. Because White's pawns commit early to dark and light squares alike, piece development has to keep pace: Black's entire counterplay aims to blow up d4 before White's king is safe. [%csl Yd4][%cal Gf8g7] }
