{ Black's bishop is on its best diagonal, eyeing d4 behind White's wall of pawns. [Nf3] is the main move, reinforcing d4 and e5 before pushing forward; [Bd3] keeps the f-pawn unblocked at first, while premature [e5] lets [b:dxe5] [w:fxe5] [Nd5] blockade the centre comfortably with the queen backing up d5. White's guiding rule here is simple: reinforce the three-pawn front with [Nf3] and a bishop before pushing [e5], so Black can never liquidate d4 on favourable terms. [%csl Yd4,Ye5,Yd5][%cal Gg1f3] }
