{ A quiet French-Sicilian hybrid: Black covers d5 before deciding between [b:d5] (transposing into the French Defence after [d4]) and [b:c5]/[b:Bb4]. White claims central space effortlessly with [d4] ([d5 e5 Nfd7] or [Bb4 e5 Ne4 Qg4]) or [Nf3]. Against [Nf3], Black can either strike with [b:d5] ([w:e5] [b:Nfd7]) into a Two Knights French or switch to [b:c5] and transpose into an Open Sicilian. [%csl Yd5][%cal Gd2d4] }
3. d4 ( 3. Nf3 ) ( 3. e5 ) ) 3. e5
