{ With [e6] guarding d5 and shutting the c4 bishop off f7, White's pawns on c5 and e5 need active piece support before [b:b6] and [b:d6] tear them apart. [Nc3] (Lasker's Simul Gambit, offering c5 after [b:Nxc3] [w:dxc3] [Bxc5] [Qg4] for a fierce kingside attack) and [d4] ([b6 cxb6 axb6]) are right, whereas early queen sorties drop the pawn for nothing. That clash between Black's unassailable d5 outpost and White's open attacking diagonals makes the Chase one of the sharpest sidelines in the Alekhine. [%csl Yd5,Yc4,Yf7][%cal Gb1c3] }
