{ Reinforcing c5 and e5 with [d4] builds an impressive diagonal chain, though Black's d5 knight sits immune to pawn attacks right in front of d4. Black chips away at the chain's flank right away with [d6] ([w:cxd6] [b:exd6] [Nf3] [Nc6]) or [b6] ([w:cxb6] [b:axb6] [Nc3] [e6]) so White's advanced pawns split into targets. Once Black chips away with [d6] or [b6], White needs fast piece development ([w:Nc3], [w:Bc4], [w:Nf3]) so the collapsing pawn wedge turns into open attacking lines. [%csl Yc5,Ye5,Yd5][%cal Gd7d6] }
