{ The Sämisch Attack develops a piece instead of pushing more pawns, offering a knight trade that drains Black's hypermodern setup of central targets. After [Nxc3] [w:dxc3], White enjoys wide-open diagonals for [w:Bc4], [w:Bf4], [w:Qe2] and [w:O-O-O] against [b:d6] or [b:e6]. Alternatively, Black can decline the trade with [e6] ([w:Nxd5] [b:exd5] [w:d4] [b:d6]) or [c6] to keep central tension in French-like fashion. [%cal Gd5c3] }
