{ Trading on c3 in the Sämisch Attack gives White two distinct recapture styles: [dxc3] opens the d-file and c1 bishop immediately for fast piece pressure ([d6 Bc4]/[Bf4] and [Qe2], with [w:O-O-O] to follow), whereas [bxc3] builds a massive central pawn mass with [d4] and [f4] against [d6] or [d5]. In the [dxc3] main line, White's fast piece activity along the open d-file and bishop diagonals compensates cleanly for the doubled queenside pawns. [%csl Yc3,Yc1][%cal Gd2c3] }
( 3... e6 ) ( 3... c6 ) 4. dxc3 ( 4. bxc3 ) ) ( 3. Bc4
