{ The St. George (or Birmingham) Defence, pioneered by Michael Basman and made famous when Tony Miles defeated World Champion Anatoly Karpov with it in 1980. Black prepares [b:b5] and [b:Bb7] to expand on the queenside, deter [w:Nc3] via [b:b4], and snipe at e4 from the flank. White claims the centre with [d4] or develops [Nf3]; [Bc4] sets a lethal trap against premove [b:b5], whereas premature [w:c4] invites [b:e5]. [%csl Ye4][%cal Gd2d4] }
