{ The Borg Defence ("Grob" spelled backwards, occasionally essayed by Michael Basman) fatally loosens Black's kingside on move one without contesting the centre. White's strongest reply is [d4], opening the c1 bishop directly onto the hanging g5 pawn! Developing [Nf3]? carelessly walks into [b:g4]. After [d4], White develops [w:Nc3], [w:Be3] and [w:Qd2] (or [w:h4] against [b:h6]), punishing Black's shattered kingside shelter with natural central moves. [%csl Yc1,Yg5][%cal Gd2d4] }
