{ The Carr Defence is a mirrored St. George that wastes a move on the kingside and slightly softens g6 should Black ever castle short. White takes the centre with [d4], forcing Black to transpose into a Pirc/Modern ([d6]/[g6]), Caro-Kann ([c6]), French ([e6]) or Creepy Crawly ([a6]). Because [h6] contributes nothing to central control, White enjoys an extra tempo in whichever Pirc, Modern, French or Caro-Kann structure Black enters next. [%csl Yg6][%cal Gd2d4] }
