{ White holds an uncontested central duo. Black should play [e6], [d6], [c6] or [g6] to contest key squares — expanding recklessly with [g5]? enters an inferior Borg Defence where White has [Nc3] and [h4] ready to rip open the kingside! Against [g6] or [d6], White's [w:Nc3], [w:Be3] and [w:Qd2] setup gains extra bite because Black's pawn on h6 already provides a direct [w:h4]-[w:h5] hook! [%csl Yh6][%cal Ge7e6] }
