{ With Black's knight centralized on e5 after trading on e5, White has three distinct plans: [Nf3] (the Paulsen Attack, offering an immediate knight swap for a clean open game where White leads slightly in development), [f4] (chasing the knight with tempo at the slight cost of loosening e1-h4), and [Nc3] (the Keres Attack, bringing out a piece first while keeping [w:f4] and [w:Qd4] in reserve). [%csl Ye5,Ye1,Yh4][%cal Gg1f3] }
