{ The de Smet Gambit sacrifices a central pawn to speed up Black's development with [exd6 Bxd6], followed by [Qe7], [Nf6], [Bg4] and queenside castling. Accepting with [exd6] is White's critical test: Black has activity but no forced knockout, so calm development with [Nc3], [Bd3] or [Be3], and [Nf3] consolidates the extra pawn cleanly. [Nf3] declines the gambit for a sound, risk-free edge after [Nf3 dxe5 Qxd8+ Kxd8]. [%csl Yd6][%cal Ge5d6,Gg1f3] }
