{ Retreating to e7 looks cramped for a single turn, yet the knight is heading straight for an active kingside post on g6, while Black's dark-squared bishop will step outside the pawn chain to c5 BEFORE Black plays [b:d6]! White's sharpest test is [Nf3 Ng6 h4] ([h5] [Bg5] [Be7]), while [c4 Ng6 Nc3 Bc5] grabs queenside space (watching out for [b:Ng4]/[b:Qh4] kingside attacks if White plays [Bd3 Nf6] and careless [Nge2]? [Ng4]!). [%csl Ye7,Yg6,Yc5][%cal Gg1f3] }
