{ Against the Harrwitz Attack ([Bf4]), Black turns to the Tartakower-style fianchetto [b6], solving the classic QGD problem of the light-squared bishop by placing it on b7 prior to striking with [b:c5]. White's most testing continuation is [cxd5] [b:Nxd5] ([b:exd5] leaves [b:c5] creating hanging pawns under heavy fire) [w:Nxd5] [b:Qxd5] [w:Bd3], racing to complete development while c7 is temporarily tender. Developing [Bd3] or [Be2] directly lets [b:Bb7] and [b:c5] equalize comfortably. [%cal Gc4d5,Gf1d3,Bc8b7] }
