{ The Cambridge Springs Defense, named after the 1904 tournament in Pennsylvania. The queen unpins the knight by counterattacking: it pins White's knight on c3, and the bishop on g5 will hang along the fifth rank once d5 opens and the knight on f3 leaves its post. [b:Ne4], [b:Bb4] and [b:dxc4] are the threats. White's best answers are [Nd2], covering e4 and c4 while breaking the pin, [cxd5], and [Bxf6]. [Bd3] holds only if White meets [b:dxc4] [w:Bxc4] [b:Ne4] by stepping the bishop off g5. [%csl Rc3,Rg5,Re4][%cal Gf3d2] }
