{ The main line. The knight covers e4 and c4, and from d2 it blocks the diagonal of Black's queen, so the knight on c3 is no longer pinned. But it has also stopped guarding g5. Black's two plans are [Bb4], adding pressure on c3 and preparing castling, and [dxc4], which opens the fifth rank toward the bishop on g5: after [dxc4], White must not take back at once, since [b:Qxg5] wins the bishop. The correct reply is [w:Bxf6], and only then [w:Nxc4], hitting the queen. [%csl Re4,Rc4,Rc3][%cal Gf8b4] }
