{ White's bishop has moved to d3, so Black should capture [dxc4] first: after [w:Bxc4] [b:b5] [w:Bd3] [b:Bb7], Black reaches the Meran a tempo up. [Nbd7] is flexible too. Pushing [b5]? before taking on c4 is a classic positional mistake: [w:c5] clamps the entire queenside shut, burying Black's bishop on c8 while White prepares [w:e4] with a free hand. [%csl Rd5][%cal Gd5c4] }
6... dxc4 ( 6... Nbd7 ) ( 6... b5 $2
