{ White develops and keeps the choice between [w:e3] and [w:Nc3]. Black's main move is [Nf6], and after [w:Nc3] Black chooses between [b:dxc4], [b:e6] and [b:a6]. [dxc4] at once lets White pick [w:e3] or [w:a4]; [e6] heads for the Semi-Slav. The order matters for the bishop on c8: it wants to come out before [e6], yet [Bf5] or [Bg4] too early runs into [w:cxd5] and [w:Qb3], hitting b7 and d5. That is why Black usually takes on c4 first or plays [e6]. [%csl Rc8,Rc4][%cal Gg8f6] }
( 3. Nc3
