{ The Schlechter Variation of the Slav, a solid Grünfeld-Slav hybrid favored by Smyslov and modern positional players alike. Black's pawn wall on c6 and d5 neutralizes White's queenside pressure, while the bishop on g7 eyes the center from safety. White develops calmly with [Bd3] or [Be2] and castles, aiming to expand slowly with [w:b3], [w:Bb2] and [w:O-O]. Clarifying with [cxd5] [b:cxd5] gives a symmetrical Carlsbad-Grünfeld structure where White retains only a tiny spatial pull. [%cal Gf1d3,Gf1e2,Bg7d4] }
