{ Bogoljubow's Variation of the Semi-Slav: instead of entering the razor-sharp Meran with [b:dxc4], Black develops [Be7] calmly to castle short and transpose toward Orthodox QGD waters. Because Black has spent a tempo on [c6] without capturing on c4, White enjoys a pleasant spatial edge. [O-O] or [Qc2] prepares the central advance [w:e4], [e4] immediately strikes while Black's king is still uncastled ([b:dxe4] [w:Nxe4] [b:Nxe4] [w:Bxe4] [b:Nf6] [w:Bc2]), and [b3] backs c4 to meet [b:O-O] with [w:Bb2] and [w:O-O]. [%cal Gd1c2,Ge3e4,Gb2b3] }
