{ White protects c4 in advance. Black's main move is [Nbd7], waiting: Black takes on c4 only after White's bishop has moved, so as to win a tempo. [a6], the Accelerated Meran, prepares [b5] at once. Black's plan is [dxc4], [b5], [Bb7] and the freeing break [c5], after which the bishop on b7 becomes one of the best pieces on the board. [%csl Rc4,Rb7][%cal Gb8d7] }
( 5. Bg5
{ The Anti-Meran Gambit: White pins the knight before playing [w:e3], inviting the sharpest battles in the Semi-Slav. [dxc4] enters the Botvinnik System, where [e4 b5 e5 h6 Bh4 g5] blows the board wide open. [h6] first asks the bishop to choose between the positional Moscow [w:Bxf6] and the sharp Anti-Moscow Gambit [w:Bh4]. [Nbd7] prepares the Cambridge Springs [b:Qa5], and [b:Be7] transposes to a quiet Orthodox. [%cal Gh7h6] }
