{ White has built a full pawn center and threatens [w:e5], winning the pinned knight on f6. Black's only consistent move is [b5], defending c4 and buying room to answer [e5 h6 Bh4 g5] in the Botvinnik main line. Passive unpinning moves like [b:Be7] let [w:Bxc4] recover the pawn with a commanding central duo while Black's light-squared bishop remains locked in. [%csl Rc4,Rc8][%cal Gb7b5] }
