{ Black supports the knight on f6 and keeps the queen free for a5. White's main move is [e3], and then Black chooses between [b:Qa5], the Cambridge Springs, and [b:Be7], an Orthodox with c6. [cxd5] [b:exd5] leads to the Exchange structure. [e4 dxe4] is a sharp try that gives Black free play. With the knight on d7, Black can meet [cxd5] with [b:exd5] without worrying about the Elephant Trap. [%csl Rf6,Ra5][%cal Ge2e3,Gc4d5] }
