{ Black has a choice of two systems. [Qa5] is the Cambridge Springs: the queen pins the knight on c3 and prepares [b:Ne4] and [b:Bb4], with ideas of [b:dxc4] against the bishop on g5. [Be7] leads to an Orthodox with the c-pawn on c6: solid, with the plan [b:O-O], [b:dxc4] and [b:Nd5]. [Bb4] mixes both ideas, while [Bd6] exposes the bishop to [w:c5] or [w:e4]. [%csl Yc3,Yg5,Yc6][%cal Gd8a5] }
