{ The Anti-Moscow Gambit: White keeps the pin on f6 and dares Black to grab c4. Accepting with [dxc4] is the critical test: after [w:e4] [b:g5] [w:Bg3] [b:b5], Black holds an extra pawn at the price of a loosened kingside and an uncastled king. [Be7] declines the gambit calmly and transposes into Orthodox Declined waters after [w:e3] [b:O-O]. Pushing [b:g5] before [dxc4] weakens the kingside without even winning a pawn. [%csl Yf6,Yc4][%cal Gd5c4] }
