( 4... b6 5. Nbd2 Bb7 6. Nc4 d5 7. Nce5 Nc6 8. Bb5
{ White's provocative knight hop via c4 to e5 and [Bb5] pin put maximum pressure on c6 while threatening [Ng5] against f7. Black's ONLY safe defense of c6 and the a4-e8 diagonal is [Qc8] (unaligning the queen from any knight forks and holding c6 firmly); trying to kick the pinning bishop with the a-pawn forgets that the e5 knight can capture c6 first! [%csl Yc6,Yf7][%cal Gd8c8] }
8... Qc8 ( 8... a6 $4
{ Chasing the bishop overlooks that TWO White pieces attack c6! [Nxc6] wins a piece or wrecks Black's queen after [Nxc6 Qd7 Nfe5 Qc8 Na7+] forking king and queen. Guard c6 accurately with [b:Qc8] instead. [%csl Yb5,Yc6][%cal Re5c6] }
