{ The Torre Attack, named after Mexican grandmaster Carlos Torre Repetto—whose famous 'windmill' combination toppled Emanuel Lasker at Moscow 1925—and favored by Tigran Petrosian and Boris Spassky. Pinning f6 restrains Black's central [e5] break while White builds [e3], [Nbd2], [Bd3], and [c3] aiming for [e4] or [Ne5]. Black answers actively with [c5], [h6], or solid [Be7] and [d5]. White keeps central tension alive. [%csl Ye4,Yb2][%cal Gc7c5,Gh7h6] }
( 3. e3
