{ Lichess Neo's coach explains these positions in its Game Review. In a comment, [Nf3] is a move, [Qb3 Qxb3 axb3] moves one after the other, [w:Re1] a later move of White, and a square is written as it is, e5. Each position's first moves are those theory goes on with. }
1. d4 d5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. e3 ( 3. Bg5
{ The Tartakower (or Classical) Torre. With d5 already on the board, White builds [e3], [Bd3], [Nbd2], and [c3]—a Colle structure where the dark-squared bishop stands actively outside the pawn chain on g5. Black can harass the bishop immediately with [Ne4] (met by [Ne4 Bf4 c5]), bring out [Bf5]—which invites [Bf5 c4 e6 Qb3] against unguarded b7—or play solid [e6] and [Be7]. [%csl Yg5][%cal Gf6e4,Ge7e6] }
3... Ne4
{ Gossip's immediate jump into e4 asks the Torre bishop an awkward question on move three before White has played [e3]. Dropping back to [Bf4] or [Be3] invites [b:c5] and [b:Qb6] targeting b2, whereas [Bh4] keeps the h4-d8 diagonal—provided White meets [Bh4 c5] with [w:e3] and [w:Nbd2] rather than letting Black trap the bishop via [b:g5]. Never leave g5 hanging to [Nxg5]. [%cal Gg5f4,Gg5h4] }
( 3... e6 4. e3 c5 5. Nbd2 ( 5. c3 Nc6
{ A classical Tartakower Torre tabiya: Black has built full Queen's Gambit Declined counterplay with [c5] and [Nc6] while White's dark-squared bishop stands outside the chain on g5. White's most accurate continuation is [Nbd2], completing queenside coordination and keeping b3 or d3 flexible while meeting [Nbd2 Qb6] cleanly with [Nbd2 Qb6 Rb1] (since b2 lacks its c1 guardian!). [Bd3] aims straight at the kingside and prepares [w:Ne5] or [w:O-O], while [Bb5] pins c6 to fight hard for the e5 outpost. [%csl Yb2][%cal Gb1d2,Gf1d3] }
6. Nbd2 ( 6. Bd3 ) ( 6. Bb5 ) ) 5... Nc6 6. c3
{ The main Classical Torre tabiya: White's c3-d4-e3 pyramid holds the center rock-solid while g5 pins f6, preparing [Bd3], [O-O], and [w:Ne5] or [Qe2] and [e4]. Black should break the pin or contest e5 first with [Be7], [Bd6], or [h6] (or poke b2 via [Qb6]), because fianchettoing on b7 before unpinning f6 leaves the c6 knight overloaded. Patience on the queenside pays off for Black. [%csl Yc6][%cal Gf8e7,Gh7h6] }
6... Be7 ( 6... Bd6 ) ( 6... Qb6 ) ( 6... h6 ) ( 6... b6 $2
