{ The Pseudo-Catalan delays [c4] to fianchetto on g2 and castle quickly, often hoping Black will lock the c8 bishop inside with a routine [e6] before White plays [c4]. Black can take full advantage of White's quiet order by bringing the bishop out first with [Bf5] or [Bg4], striking at the center with [c5], building a Slav wall with [c6] (keeping c8 open), or mirroring symmetrically with [g6]. [%cal Gc8f5,Gc7c5,Gc7c6] }
