{ Armand Blackmar's original 1882 gambit move order, still played in over two million online games! Offering [f3] on move three before [w:Nc3] lets Black return the extra pawn immediately with [e5]: after [e5 dxe5 Qxd1+ Kxd1 Nc6], Black trades queens, displaces White's king on d1, and regains e5 smoothly ([exf3 Nxf3] and [Nf6 Nc3] transpose back to the main Blackmar-Diemer). [%cal Ge7e5,Ge4f3,Gg8f6] }
