4... d6 ( 4... O-O ) ( 4... c5 ) ( 4... d5 ) ) 4... d6
{ The main starting point of the King's Indian Defence. Black halts [e5] and prepares to castle and strike at d4 with [b:e5] or [b:c5]. White has a rich menu of fifth moves: [Nf3] heads into the Classical System, [f3] is the rock-solid Sämisch Variation, [Be2] sets up the Averbakh ([Be2 O-O Bg5]) or Semi-Averbakh ([Be2 O-O Be3]), [h3] is the modern Makogonov System, and [f4] launches the all-out Four Pawns Attack. [%csl Yd4][%cal Gg1f3] }
