{ Black castles before playing [d6], inviting White to push [e5] prematurely. If White takes the bait with [e5], Black retreats [e5 Ne8] and undermines the advanced pawns with [d6] and [b:c5], as Bobby Fischer famously did against René Letelier at the 1960 Leipzig Olympiad. White does better to develop calmly with [Nf3], [Be2], [Be3] or [f3], when Black almost always plays [d6] next. [%cal Gg1f3] }
