{ Black plants a bold outpost knight on d4 supported by the e5-pawn and g7-bishop. White's essential move is [Nge2], challenging the intruder with a knight ([Nge2 c5 dxc6 bxc6 Nxd4 exd4 Bxd4] is safe once [Nge2] is in, whereas castling long immediately walks into [b:c5] and [b5] against White's king). Snatching d4 right away with [Bxd4] loses badly along the e-file and long diagonal. [%csl Yd4][%cal Gg1e2] }
