12... Nfxe4 13. Nxe4 Nxe4 ) ) ( 8... a6 ) 9. h3
{ The Classical Fianchetto Main Line. With [h3] on the board, White rules out [Ng4] and [Bg4] forever and prepares [Be3], [Qc2] and [w:Rfd1] for a harmonious squeeze. Black must create active counter-pressure against d4 and e4: [Qb6] eyes d4 and b2 ([Qb6 Re1 exd4 Nxd4 Re8]), [Qa5] pins c3 along the diagonal so [Qa5 Re1 exd4 Nxd4 Ne5] hits c4, and [Re8] or [a5] keeps the tension. [%csl Yd4,Ye4,Yb2][%cal Gd8b6] }
( 9. Re1 ) ( 9. Qc2 ) ( 9. Bg5 $6
