{ Black develops the queen's knight to c6, increasing pressure on d4 and preparing [b:dxc4] followed by [b:e5] or [b:Bd6] in Ragozin fashion. White has four solid options: [a3] forces the b4-bishop to trade [a3 Bxc3] or retreat [a3 Be7] right away (since [b:Ba5] is trapped by [w:b4]), [Rc1] contests the c-file, [cxd5] clarifies the center with [cxd5 exd5 Bd3], and [Bd3] prepares castling. [%csl Yc6,Yd4][%cal Ga2a3] }
