8. b4 Nxb4 9. axb4 ) ) ) ( 6. Qc2
{ White protects c3 with the queen so [w:a3] will win the bishop pair without doubling the c-pawns, while lining up toward h7 once the center opens and clearing d1 for a rook. Black's sharpest counterplay is [c5], striking at d4 before White castles, or [b6] preparing [b:Bb7] and [b:Nbd7] to hold e4. Hopping into e4 prematurely only helps White gain time with the bishops. [%csl Yc3,Yh7,Yd1][%cal Gc7c5] }
