{ The Deferred Sämisch: White forces the b4-bishop to declare its intentions right away. Because White has already placed the knight on f3 blocking the f-pawn, White can no longer build the fast f3-e4 pawn roller of the pure Sämisch, so Black gladly trades [Bxc3+] and strikes at the center with [Bxc3+ bxc3 c5] (or retreats [Be7] into a solid Queen's Gambit Declined). Retreating to a5 walks into a bishop trap. [%csl Yf3,Ya5][%cal Gb4c3] }
