{ Viswanathan Anand's favorite counterattack in the Open Catalan: instead of clinging to c4, Black strikes at d4 right away to trade off White's central pawn and neutralize White's space advantage. White usually castles with [O-O], after which [O-O Nc6 Qa4 Bd7 Qxc4 b5] regains the pawn with sharp play, while [O-O Nc6 dxc5 Qxd1 Rxd1 Bxc5 Nbd2] reaches a deceptive queenless middlegame where White's g2-bishop presses Black's queenside. [Qa4+] is a quieter way to recover c4. [%csl Yc4,Yd4][%cal Ge1g1] }
