4... Bb4+ ) ( 4... c6 ) ( 4... c5
{ The Tarrasch Defense to the Catalan, an active way to fight for equality if Black is willing to play with an isolated queen's pawn. White's two best replies are [cxd5], when [cxd5 exd5 Nf3 Nc6 O-O Be7] reaches the Rubinstein-Tarrasch battle where White's g2-bishop bears down directly on the isolated d5-pawn, and [Nf3] keeping central tension. Developing [w:Nc3] before [w:Nf3], however, lets Black liquidate the center on favorable terms. [%cal Gc4d5] }
