{ The Closed Catalan. Black refuses to open the long diagonal for White's g2-bishop and builds a sturdy Semi-Slav pawn triangle on c6, d5 and e6. Black's camp is rock-solid, at the price of shutting in the light-squared bishop on c8: freeing that bishop via [b:b6], [b:Bb7] (or [b:Ba6]) and a later [b:c5] break is Black's main strategic task. White's standard move is [Qc2], guarding c4 and preparing [w:Rd1], [w:Nbd2] and [w:e4]. [%csl Yc6,Yd5,Ye6][%cal Gd1c2] }
