7... Qxd4 8. Qxd4 Bxd4 ) ) 6... O-O 7. O-O
{ Both kings are castled and the central standoff begins. Black's knight on d5 cannot stay undefended forever once White plays [w:Nc3] and [e4], so [Nb6] is the classic retreat, keeping the long diagonal clear for the g7-bishop before developing [b:Nc6] to pile up on d4 and prepare [b:e5] or [b:Bg4]. [c5] challenges d4 immediately, while [Nc6] pressures d4 without retreating the d5-knight first. [%csl Yd5,Yd4][%cal Gd5b6,Bc7c5,Yb8c6] }
