{ The classical Neo-Grünfeld tabiya (Carlsen-Giri, Wijk aan Zee 2011). Black's knight on c6 and bishop on g7 team up on d4, forcing White to act. Pushing [d5] kicks the knight to a5 or e5, after which Black chips at the advanced pawn with [b:c6]. Quietly defending with [e3] holds d4 rock-solid and invites [b:Re8] and [b:e5], where Black breaks in the center and eyes the d3 and c4 outposts. [%csl Yc6,Yg7,Yd4][%cal Gd4d5,Be2e3] }
