{ The Early Neo-Grünfeld with [Nf3]: Black challenges the center on move three before fianchettoing, inviting White to clarify the central tension while the queenside knight still sits at home. [Nc3] transposes directly into the Three Knights Grünfeld ([Nc3 Bg7]), whereas [cxd5 Nxd5] lets White chase the knight immediately with [w:e4] without allowing doubled c-pawns. [g3] and [e3] keep solid Catalan- and Schlechter-like structures open. [%cal Gb1c3,Bc4d5,Yg2g3] }
4. Nc3 ( 4. cxd5 ) ( 4. g3 ) ( 4. e3 ) ) 4. g3 O-O 5. Bg2 d5
