( 5... c6 6. O-O d5
{ The Classical Neo-Grünfeld (Original Defense). By inserting [c6] before pushing [d5], Black guarantees a sturdy pawn foothold on d5 so White can never force Black's knight into the middle. Because c4 is now genuinely attacked by d5, White must address the pawn: [cxd5 cxd5] enters the symmetrical Carlsbad-fianchetto main line, while [b3] and [Nbd2] defend c4 to keep tension alive ([Nc3] gambits or invites [Nc3 dxc4]). [%csl Yd5,Yc4][%cal Gc4d5,Bb2b3,Yb1d2] }
