{ The Ultra-Delayed Exchange tabiya of the Neo-Grünfeld. Both sides have identical pawn islands and open c-files, so the fight turns on the e5 and e4 outposts and the c8-bishop. White's most testing move is [Ne5], planting the knight in the middle and unleashing the g2-bishop against d5 (which Black meets with [Ne5 Bf5] or [Ne5 e6]), while [Bf4] controls e5 and c7 before Black's bishop leaves home. [%csl Ye5,Ye4,Yd5][%cal Gf3e5,Bc1f4] }
