{ The Accelerated Russian System, played by Euwe against Alekhine in their 1935 World Championship match. White piles three attackers onto d5 before developing [Nf3], practically forcing [dxc4 Qxc4] so White can follow with [w:e4] and [w:Bf4]. Because White's g1-knight is not yet on f3, Black has extra flexibility after [dxc4 Qxc4 Bg7]: Black can build a solid wall with [b:c6] and [b:Be6] without worrying about an early [Ng5], or transpose into the main Russian lines after [w:Nf3] and [b:O-O]. [%csl Yd5,Yf3][%cal Gd5c4,Bc7c6] }
