{ White's broad c3-d4-e4 pawn mass now dominates the center, guarded from behind by the c3-pawn, while White's c1-bishop enjoys an open diagonal toward the kingside. Black immediately fianchettoes with [Bg7], aiming directly down the long diagonal through d4 and c3 toward White's rook on a1; [c5] right away is a sharp move-order alternative that reaches the same tabiya once [b:Bg7] follows. [%csl Yd4,Yc3,Ya1][%cal Gf8g7,Bc7c5] }
