{ The Classical Exchange Variation. Putting the bishop on c4 eyes f7 (which stops an immediate [b:Bg4] trick later) and, crucially, leaves e2 free for White's g1-knight: from e2, the knight guards d4 and c3 without ever getting pinned by [b:Bg4], allowing White to meet [b:Bg4] cleanly with [w:f3]. Black strikes at d4 with [c5] or castles first with [O-O] (usually transposing on the next move). [%csl Yc4,Yf7,Ye2][%cal Gc7c5,Be8g8] }
