{ Once the bishop drops back to d3, Black must liquidate the tension on d4 with [cxd4 cxd4 Be6], seizing control of the newly weakened c4 outpost and daring White to sacrifice the exchange with [w:d5] ([b:Bxa1] [w:Qxa1]) for a dark-square attack. Pushing [c4] instead closes the queenside prematurely and takes all pressure off White's central duo, leaving White free to prepare [w:e5] and [w:f4] at leisure. [%csl Yd3,Yd4,Yc4][%cal Gc5d4] }
