{ Karpov's solid [Be3] Exchange System. White reinforces d4 and controls c5 first, preparing [w:Qd2] plus [w:Rc1] (or [w:Rb1]) before deciding where the g1-knight and f1-bishop belong. That flexible move order avoids early pins from [b:Bg4] while taking the sting out of [b:Bxc3+] checks. Black still strikes immediately with [c5], and after [c5 Qd2 Qa5 Rc1 O-O Nf3 Rd8], both sides maneuver around d4 in a deep strategic fight. [%csl Yd4,Yc5][%cal Gc7c5,Be8g8] }
