{ The Huisl Variation, championed by Simon Williams. Black plants the knight on e4 right away to disrupt White's [Re1]+[w:e4] plan. White's main replies are [Qc2] ([Qc2 Nxc3 Qxc3 a5] or [b:Bf6], fighting for e5) and [Nxe4 fxe4 Nd2 d5], where Black transforms into an improved Stonewall with the f-file already open! Pushing [d5] without trading on e4 hands Black easy play. [%csl Ye4,Ye5][%cal Gd1c2,Bc3e4] }
