{ Black strikes at White's broad three-pawn front with [e5], opening the f8-bishop and clearing the d8-h4 diagonal for Black's queen. White has only one sound response: capture en passant with [dxe6] ([dxe6 fxe6] or [dxe6 dxe6]), keeping the e1-h4 diagonal shielded while challenging Black's center. Both [f5] and [fxe5] — played in thousands of club games — walk straight into a devastating queen check on h4. [%cal Gd5e6,Gd8h4] }
