{ The Lithuanian Variation of the Mikenas Defence. Black strikes at d4 immediately on move two before developing the kingside knight. White's principled reply is [d5], chasing the knight to e7 ([d5 Nce7], heading for g6, [b:Bc5] and [b:d6] plus [b:f5], whereas [d5 Nd4] is the tricky Cannstatter sideline), while [dxe5 Nxe5] gives Black open piece play. Carelessly developing [Nc3] drops d4 at once. [%cal Gd4d5,Ge5d4,Gc6d4] }
