3... Nxd4 4. Nf3 Nc6 ) 3... Nce7
{ The main Lithuanian tabiya. Black's knight retreats to e7 on its way to g6, clearing the f8-bishop for c5 or b4 while preparing [b:Nf6], [b:d6] and an eventual King's-Indian-style [b:f5] counterattack. White builds a commanding spatial wedge with [Nc3] and [e4] (or h4 in modern engine lines to harass the g6-knight), aiming to break through on the queenside with [w:b4] and [w:c5] before Black's kingside play arrives. [%csl Ye7,Yg6,Yc5][%cal Gb1c3,Be2e4] }
