{ The Rat (or Pirc/Old Indian) move order. By starting with d6 on move one, Black invites White to push [e4] and cross into King's Pawn openings via the Pirc ([e4 Nf6]) or Philidor ([e4 e5] and [e4 Nd7]). Dedicated Queen's Pawn players usually decline that invitation with [c4] (steering toward Old Indian, King's Indian or Rat lines) or [Nf3], where Black has the independent Wade Defence [Nf3 Bg4]. [%cal Ge2e4,Gc2c4,Gg1f3] }
