( 2. e4 ) ( 2. Nf3
{ White develops the king's knight first, controlling e5 and d4 while keeping [c4], [e4], [Bf4] and quiet Colle or Torre setups in reserve. Black almost always fianchettoes with [Bg7], waiting to see White's pawn structure before choosing between [d6], [c5] and [Nf6]. Playing [Nf6] immediately transposes back into standard King's Indian and Grünfeld move orders, whereas [d5] stakes a solid central foothold right away so Black can follow up with [Bg7] and [c6]. [%csl Yd4,Ye5][%cal Gg1f3] }
