{ A quiet Colle / Zukertort setup against the Modern fianchetto. By playing e3, White keeps d4 rock-solid, prepares quick kingside castling with [w:Be2] or [w:Bd3], and often follows up with a queenside fianchetto ([w:b3] and [w:Bb2]) to oppose Black's g7-bishop down the long diagonal. Black has an easy game with [Nf6] (heading toward King's Indian or Neo-Grünfeld structures), [d6] (preparing [b:Nd7] and [b:e5]), or the immediate hypermodern strike [c5]. [%cal Gf1d3,Gb2b3,Gg8f6,Gc7c5] }
