{ The Pterodactyl Variation against the Colle System. Black brings the queen out early to a5 with check to disrupt White's routine Colle setup and coordinate with the g7-bishop down the long diagonal. Interposing [Bd2] is White's strongest reply: after [Bd2 Qd8] (since [Bd2 Qb6 Nc3] gives White dangerous rapid development even if Black snatches b2), White keeps a clean developmental lead; [Nc3] and [Nbd2] also block the check comfortably. [%cal Gc1d2,Gb1c3,Gg7b2,Ra5e1] }
