{ The Neo-Modern fianchetto: Black delays developing g8 to f6, keeping the g7-bishop's long diagonal completely unobstructed and reserving direct central strikes like [b:c5], [b:d6] plus [b:e5], or [b:Nc6]. White usually seizes the whole center with [Nc3] and [e4]—forcing Black to counterpunch accurately before getting overrun—or develops [Nf3] first to rule out early [b:c5] doubled-pawn Pterodactyl lines in advance. [%cal Gb1c3,Ge2e4] }
