{ The Budapest Gambit, first played by Géza Maróczy against Mór Adler in Budapest in 1896 and propelled to fame at Berlin 1918 when Milan Vidmar crushed Akiba Rubinstein in 24 moves. Black sacrifices the e-pawn to shatter White's d4-c4 center and gain rapid piece play. Accepting with [dxe5] is the only way to test the gambit; declining hands Black effortless equality or an active initiative. [%cal Gd4e5] }
