{ Black checks on b4 before playing [b:Qe7] so the dark-squared bishop is not locked in on f8. White reaches the fundamental crossroads of the Rubinstein Budapest: [Nbd2] is the positional main line (championed by Rubinstein and Karpov, returning e5 cleanly to keep healthy pawns and win the bishop pair), while [Nc3] is the critical pawn-keeping try (Gligorić and Seirawan's line, accepting doubled c-pawns after [Nc3 Bxc3+ bxc3 Qe7 Qd5]). [%csl Yb4,Yf8,Ye5][%cal Gb1d2,Bb1c3] }
