{ Even after trading one pair of knights on e5, the Kieninger mate trap is still cocked and loaded because Black's e7-queen still pins White's e2-pawn to the king! White must unpin calmly with [e3], forcing [e3 Bxd2+ Qxd2 d6] (note [b:Ba5] gets trapped by [w:b4], and [b:b6] runs into [w:Qd5]) with the bishop pair and a lasting positional pull. Taking b4 still gets mated in one. [%csl Ye5,Yb4][%cal Ge2e3] }
