9... Nd3# ) ) ( 2... d6
{ The Old Indian Defence, coined by Savielly Tartakower in the 1920s. Unlike the King's Indian ([b:g6] and [b:Bg7]), Black keeps the kingside pawns unmoved (g7-f7-h7 without a hook on g6) and develops the dark-squared bishop modestly to e7 while striking at the center with [b:e5] and [b:Nbd7] (or [b:Bf5] in Janowski's line). Note that [Nc3 g6] transposes into the King's Indian, whereas [Nc3 e5] and [Nc3 Nbd7] stay in pure Old Indian territory. [%csl Yg6,Ye7][%cal Gb1c3,Bg1f3] }
