{ The Slav-Indian. Black plays [c6] before [b:d5], keeping every Slav and Semi-Slav door open if White develops [Nc3], [Nf3] or [Bf4] (met by [b:d5] or [b:Qb6]), while also reserving Schlechter-Grünfeld and King's Indian transpositions via [b:g6]. If White pushes [d5] impatiently on move three, Black trades [d5 cxd5 cxd5] and undermines the advanced pawn comfortably with [b:e6], [b:b5] or [b:Qa5+]. [%cal Gb1c3,Bg1f3,Yc1f4] }
