{ By developing [Nf3] on move three against the Black Knights' Tango, White stops Black's dream [b:e5] central break in its tracks. Black responds with the flexible [e6], keeping Nimzo-Indian ([e6 Nc3 Bb4]), Bogo-Indian ([e6 g3 Bb4+]) and Georgi Orlov's King's-Indian-style Tango ([e6 a3 d6] followed by [b:g6] and [b:Bg7]) all on the table, while [d6] prepares a delayed [b:e5] directly. [%cal Ge7e6,Bd7d6] }
( 3. Nc3
