{ White kicks the c6-knight immediately, and Black's knight hops into the middle to attack the undefended c4-pawn. White usually defends c4 and claims the center with [e4], which Black challenges straight away with [e4 e6] to open the b4-check diagonal and fight for dark squares ([Nc3] and [Nf3] are solid positional alternatives, while the sharp Horsefly Gambit [f4] is best met by [f4 Nxc4]). [%cal Ge5c4,Ge2e4,Ge7e6] }
