{ The Pyrenees Gambit: Black offers a wing pawn on move two, hoping White plays passively so Black can trade on c4 in Benko-like fashion without allowing d5. White's principled refutation is simply [cxb5], pocketing the pawn while keeping d4 and e4 ready ([cxb5 a6 e3] or [cxb5 e6 Nc3]). Declining with routine moves (e3, c5 or Nf3) lets Black equalize on the spot. [%csl Yc4,Yd4,Ye4][%cal Gc4b5] }
