{ The Anglo-Grünfeld: Black centralizes the knight on d5 without having spent a move on [b:g6] yet. White has three strong continuations: [g3] prepares [w:Bg2] to force Black's knight to declare itself ([g3 g6 Bg2 Nb6] or [b:Nxc3]); [Nf3] develops while keeping [e4], [d4] and [g3] open; and [e4] forces [e4 Nxc3 bxc3] (or [e4 Nb4 Bc4]), claiming a broad central pawn duo supported by the open b-file. [%csl Yd5][%cal Gg2g3,Bg1f3,Ye2e4] }
( 3... Qxd5 $4
