{ The Hedgehog setup, one of modern chess's deepest strategic systems. Once White opens the center with [d4 cxd4 Qxd4] (or recaptures with the knight), Black tucks pawns along the sixth rank on a6, b6, d6 and e6 with [Qc7], [Nbd7] and rooks on c8 and e8. Behind those 'spines' Black has zero weaknesses and waits like a coiled spring for the two classic liberations, [b5] on the queenside or [d5] in the center, while White maneuvers with [Re1], [b3] and [Bb2] to restrain both breaks. [%cal Gd2d4] }
