{ The English Four Knights, one of the richest tabiyas in the entire opening. Every minor knight is on its natural post, and White chooses the structure of the middlegame: [g3] fianchettoes for a long-range battle over d5 and d4; [e3], favored by Garry Kasparov, prepares [d4] or [Qc2] while keeping the position compact; [e4] locks a grip on d5 at the cost of a hole on d4; [d4] opens a reversed Four Knights Scotch right away, and [a3] prepares [b4] before Black can pin with [Bb4]. [%csl Yd5,Yd4][%cal Gg2g3,Be2e3,Ye2e4] }
