{ From's Gambit, named after 19th-century Danish master Severin From: Black sacrifices a central pawn on move one to exploit the e1-h4 diagonal weakened by [f4]! Accepting with [fxe5] is White's critical and objectively strongest choice, holding a clear advantage with accurate defense ([fxe5 d6 exd6 Bxd6 Nf3]); aggressive players also sidestep From's lines by pushing [e4] into the double-edged King's Gambit. [%csl Ye1,Yh4][%cal Gf4e5] }
