{ Black's most principled reply: [e5] stakes a claim in the center and immediately uncovers the f8 bishop's attack on the unguarded b4 pawn! [Bb2] is the true Orangutan continuation, counterattacking e5 along the long diagonal so both pawns hang at once; [a3] defends b4 conservatively first, letting Black develop comfortably with [d5] or [Nf6]. That immediate clash between Black's central pawn and White's wing pawn gives the Orangutan its unmistakable character, forcing concrete calculation from move two onward. [%csl Yf8,Yb4,Ye5][%cal Gc1b2,Ba2a3] }
