{ Occupying the center without guarding e5 first hands White a free central pawn after [Nxe5 Bd6 d4], leaving White with both extra material and a comfortable fianchetto. Push [b:e4] first if you want [b:d5] next! [%csl Re5][%cal Gf3e5] }
3. Nxe5 Bd6 4. d4 ) ( 2... Qf6 $2
{ Defending e5 with the queen takes away the f6 square from Black's own knight and exposes the queen to [Nc3] and [w:Nd5] jumps: after [Nc3 Nc6 Bg2], White's knight leaps into d5 with tempo against the queen and c7. Guard e5 naturally with [Nc6] or push [b:e4] instead. [%csl Re5,Rf6,Rd5,Rc7][%cal Gb1c3] }
