3. exf5 exf5 4. Bg2 ) ) ) 2. Bg2
{ White puts the sniper on g2 before showing any central pawn or knight. Black's most ambitious reply is [e5], building a full classical two-pawn center that White immediately chips at from the flank with [c4] or [d3] and [Nf3]. Solid players prefer [c6] (walling off g2 before [Bf5] or [Bg4]) or [Nf6] and [c5]. Whichever structure Black builds, White's g2 bishop stands ready to rake the center and queenside the moment [c4] or [e4] chips away at Black's central pawns. [%csl Yg2][%cal Ge7e5,Bg8f6,Yc7c6] }
( 2. Nf3 ) 2... e5
{ Reversed Modern Defence: Black accepts White's hypermodern invitation and builds an ideal classical center on d5 and e5. White must strike at that pawn mass before Black consolidates it, either chipping immediately from the wing with [c4] so the g2 bishop rakes d5 and b7, or playing [d3] followed by [w:Nf3] (or [w:Nd2] and [w:e4]) in Pirc and Modern reversed fashion. [%csl Yd5,Ye5][%cal Gc2c4,Bd2d3] }
( 2... Nf6
