{ The Nimzowitsch-Larsen Attack, pioneered by Aron Nimzowitsch in the 1920s, turned into an elite weapon by Bent Larsen between 1968 and 1972, and adopted five times by Bobby Fischer in 1970. White prepares [Bb2] to rake d4 and e5 and x-ray g7 down the long dark-squared diagonal, while keeping the f-pawn unblocked so [f4] remains ready against Black's center. Black's main replies are [e5] (the Modern Variation, blocking the diagonal directly), [d5] (the Classical Variation), [Nf6] (the Indian Variation) and [c5]. [%csl Yd4,Ye5,Yg7][%cal Ge7e5,Bd7d5] }
