{ The King's Indian Attack (also called the Barcza System after Hungarian GM Gedeon Barcza): White heads straight for [Bg2] and short castling, waiting to see how Black arranges the center before choosing between [d3] with [Nbd2] and [e4] (Fischer's kingside attacking setup), [c4] (Réti/Catalan play), or [w:d4] (Reversed Grünfeld). Black's main setups are [Nf6] with [c6] (building a granite wall against g2), [c5] claiming space, and Keres's [Bg4]. [%csl Yg2][%cal Gg8f6,Bc7c5,Yc8g4] }
