{ White opens the f1 bishop's diagonal to pick up c4 effortlessly while keeping the option of [b3] and [Bb2] or a later [d4]. Black's soundest response is to return the pawn and develop with [Nf6] ([Nf6 Bxc4 e6]) or strike at the center with [c5] ([c5 Bxc4 e6]). [Be6] is Keres's tricky attempt to guard c4 with a piece, while [b5] tries to hold the pawn on the wing: requiring exact defense after [b5 a4]! [%csl Yf1,Yc4][%cal Gg8f6,Bc7c5,Ye7e6] }
