{ Anderssen's Opening, played three times by Adolf Anderssen against Paul Morphy in their famous 1858 Paris match! Essentially a clever waiting move, [a3] passes the first-move initiative to Black in hopes of reaching a defense with colors reversed where a3 stops [Bb4] or prepares [b4]: such as [e5 c4] (a Reversed Paulsen/Kan Sicilian). Black does best to play [d5], [g6] (blunting any [b4] and [Bb2] idea) or [Nf6], where a3 brings White little value. [%csl Ya3][%cal Gd7d5,Bg7g6,Ye7e5] }
