{ The Shy Attack: White tucks every piece behind the third rank with a kingside fianchetto framed by [a3] and [h3], avoiding all early contact in reversed Hippopotamus / Philidor fashion. Because White applies zero pressure on d5 or e5, Black stands comfortably ahead in space and completes an ideal central setup with [Be6] and [Re8] (or [Bf5] eyeing d3), keeping [b:Qd7] and a well-timed [b:e4] or [b:d4] break in hand. [%csl Yd3][%cal Gc8e6,Bf8e8,Yc8f5] }
