{ The Ware (or Meadow Hay) Opening, named after 19th-century American player Preston Ware and once used as a blitz joke by Magnus Carlsen against Teimour Radjabov at the 2012 World Blitz Championship. Pushing [a4] neither fights for the center nor frees a minor piece, and early rook lifts backfire fast. Black seizes the center with [e5] (eyeing a3 with the f8 bishop!) or [d5]. [%csl Ya3,Yf8][%cal Ge7e5,Bd7d5,Yg8f6] }
