1... c6 2. Bb2
{ In the Outflank Variation after [Bb2], White's bishop claims the long diagonal toward e5 and g7, while Black's c6 pawn prepares both central expansion and immediate queenside counterplay. Black's cleanest continuation is [d5] (transposing into the solid Slav-wall Sokolsky where [b:Bf5] or [b:Bg4] follows), [Qb6] hitting both b4 and b2 to provoke [Qb6 a3] before [b:d5], or a flexible [d6] preparing [b:e5]. [%csl Ye5][%cal Gd7d5,Bd8b6,Yd7d6] }
