{ Bugayev's Advance Variation: once Tartakower's [f6] blunts the b2 bishop and keeps b4 under attack from f8, White pushes [b5] to dodge the capture while cramping Black's queenside and taking away c6. Black's cleanest counterplay is striking straight down the middle with [d5] (building an unchallenged central wedge after [d5 e3 Be6] or [d5 e3 Bd6]), chipping at the advanced pawn with [a6], or developing [Bc5]. [%csl Yc6][%cal Gd7d5,Ba7a6,Yf8c5] }
