{ Santasiere's Folly: combining Zukertort knight control via [Nf3] over e5 with the Orangutan flank push [b4] against [d5], colorful New York master Anthony Santasiere aimed for [w:Bb2], [w:e3] and [w:c4] to chip away at Black's center from the queenside. Black develops naturally with [Nf6] (aiming for [b:Bf5], [b:Bg4] or [b:e6] and [b:c5]), plays [e6] opening the f8 bishop against b4, or brings out [Nc6]. [%csl Ye5][%cal Gg8f6,Be7e6,Yb8c6] }
