{ White puts the bishop on the long diagonal while keeping [w:g5] ready if Black carelessly plays [Nf6]. Black's strongest plan is [d5] followed by [c6] (blunting g2 and dominating the middle), or [Nc6] and [Ne7] heading toward g6 and the permanent f4 hole without ever giving White the [w:g5] tempo. White's only compensation for the airy kingside lies in active pressure down the h1-a8 diagonal, which White tries to stoke with [c4] and [Qb3] against Black's queenside. [%csl Yg2,Yg6,Yf4,Yh1][%cal Gd7d5] }
