{ The Double Grob: Black mirrors White's reckless wing thrust, keeping symmetry at the price of exposing Black's own kingside! White gets an easy advantage simply by occupying the center with [d4] (uncovering an attack on the unguarded g5 pawn!) or fianchettoing with [Bg2], whereas the internet meme 'Coca-Cola Gambit' [f4] shreds White's own king shelter! In either sensible continuation White uses the first-move tempo to grab central squares and target Black's loosened f5 and h5 holes while keeping White's own king out of firing lines. [%csl Yg5,Yf5,Yh5][%cal Gd2d4,Bf1g2] }
